hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19201","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 1020 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he sees it is a lie, he is one of the liars - or he said: the lying ones."""
"19202","1021 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he sees it is a lie, he is one of the lying ones."""
"19203","1022 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he sees it is a lie, he is one of the lying ones."""
"19204","Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi from al-Mughirah. 1023 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Qabisah - and once he said: from Qabisah ibn Jabir - from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) holding the waist-wrapper of Sufyan ibn Sahl - and he is the son of Abu Sahl - while he was saying: ""Do not let your lower garment hang down, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang down."""
"19205","1024 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Uqbah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take hold of the cloak of Sufyan ibn Sahl while he was saying: ""O Sufyan, do not let it hang down, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang down."" Thus Yazid ibn Harun narrated it from Sharik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Uqbah; and Sufyan said: Ibn Sahl."
"19206","al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd from al-Mughirah. 1025 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, (H) and Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Talib narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn A'ishah narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The watchword of my ummah upon the Bridge is: Grant safety, grant safety."""
"19207","1026 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The watchword of my ummah upon the Bridge is: O Lord, grant safety."""
"19208","1027 - Bishr ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise, and they will be called in Paradise: the Hell-dwellers; they will supplicate to Allah to remove that name from them, and Allah will remove it from them when they have come out of the Fire."" And he mentioned the hadith."
"19209","Narration of the Basrans from al-Mughirah. Fadalalah ibn Amr al-Zahrani from al-Mughirah. 1028 - Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Fadalalah ibn Amr al-Zahrani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19210","1029 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Fadalalah ibn Amr al-Zahrani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his dwelling, and I followed him. He said: ""Where did you leave the people?"" I said: I left them at such-and-such place. He made his camel kneel and dismounted, then went and hid from me, remaining about as long as a man takes to relieve himself, then came and said: ""Do you have water with you?"" I said: Yes. I poured upon his hands, he washed his face and hands, wiped his head - and he was wearing a Syrian cloak whose sleeves had become tight - so he put his hand in from under the cloak, raised it from his hands, then washed his hands and face, wiped his head and his leather socks, then said: ""Do you have a need?"" I said: No. He said: So we rode until we caught up with the people."
"19211","Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi from al-Mughirah. 1030 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his forelock and his turban, and wiped over his leather socks, and I witnessed that."
"19212","1031 - Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: Two traits I shall not ask anyone about after witnessing them with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): wiping over the leather socks, and the prayer of an imam behind one of his subjects. We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey and dismounted at a stop; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went aside for some need. When he had relieved himself I brought him water, he performed ablution ... and wiped over his forelock, his turban and his leather socks. Then we came to the people while they were praying, and the people had put Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf forward; we caught a rak'ah with them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made up the other rak'ah."
"19213","1032 - Amr ibn Thawr al-Judhami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, (H) and Umar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I reached with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; he stepped back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signaled to him, so we prayed what we caught and made up what we had missed."
"19214","1033 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (H) and Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubaydah al-Askari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; at dawn I spurred my camel and came alongside him, and he went on until he disappeared from me. Then he came and said: ""Your need?"" I said: I have no need. He said: ""Do you have water with you?"" I said: Yes. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then went on until he caught up with the people while they were praying, with Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf leading them; he stirred at the coming of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he signaled with his hand to Abd al-Rahman to remain firm. We prayed what we caught and made up what we had missed."
"19215","1034 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Wahb - or Ibn Wahb - from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: Two traits I shall never abandon: to wipe over my leather socks, and to pray behind a man of my subjects; and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the leather socks and pray behind Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf."""
"19216","1035 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib and Hisham, (H) and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham and Ayyub and Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I poured water upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, washed his face and forearms, wiped his forelock and over the turban and the leather socks."
"19217","1036 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, (H) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Awf and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi narrated to us that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his forelock, his turban and his leather socks."
"19218","1037 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Bahrani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman the brother of Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he poured upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a waterskin; he said: So he performed ablution and washed his face - and he was wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves - he brought his hands out, washed them, wiped over his turban and his leather socks; and we came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf while he was praying, having prayed a rak'ah with them, so we prayed with him the rak'ah we caught and made up the rak'ah we had missed."""
"19219","1038 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Habib al-Adawi narrated to us, Salm ibn Sulayman Abu Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Hurrah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."
"19220","1039 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from a man kunya Abu Abdullah, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, he said: I asked al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Did any of the Companions besides Abu Bakr lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer? He said: Yes. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on such-and-such a journey; near dawn he struck the neck of my camel, turned aside and I turned with him, relieved himself, then said: ""O Mughirah, do you have a need?"" I said: I have no need. He said: ""Is there any water?"" So he called for a waterskin or a water vessel, washed his hands and face, then went to uncover his forearms but the sleeve of a Syrian cloak he was wearing was tight, so he brought his hands out from under the cloak, washed his hands, wiped his forelock and wiped over the leather socks. He said: Then we reached the people while the prayer had been established and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading them, having prayed a rak'ah with them; I went to inform him and he forbade me. We prayed what we caught and made up what we had missed."
"19221","1040 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, the like of it."
"19222","1041 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from one of his companions, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured water, washed his hands then washed his face; when he intended to wash his forearms he was wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, so he brought his hands out from under the cloak, washed his forearms, then wiped his forelock, wiped his head and over his turban and his leather socks."
"19223","Jubayr ibn Hayyah al-Thaqafi, their freedman, from al-Mughirah. 1042 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father Jubayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said - and I think the family of Ziyad informed me that he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""The rider walks behind the funeral, the walker walks behind it and to its right and to its left; and the miscarried fetus is prayed over and supplication for forgiveness and mercy for its parents is made for it."""
"19224","1043 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The miscarried fetus is prayed over and supplication is made for its parents for well-being and mercy."" Sufyan did not raise it."
"19225","1044 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bukayr al-Muzani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The rider is behind the funeral, the walker wherever he wishes of it, and the child is prayed over."""
"19226","1045 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (H) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Ubaydullah, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The rider is behind the funeral, the walker wherever he wishes, and the child is prayed over."""
"19227","1046 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Sa'id ibn Ubaydullah ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah narrated to us, from his father, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The rider is behind the funeral, the walker wherever he wishes, and the child is prayed over."""
"19228","1047 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, (H) and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Sa'id al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are aided through them."""
"19229","1048 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah, he said: I prayed beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he smelled garlic from me. He said: ""What is this smell?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I complained of my chest and ate it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not disapprove of it."
"19230","1049 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, he said: Bandadqan the non-Arab sent to them: Send, O Arabs, a man of you whom we may address. The people chose al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. My father said: It is as if I see him now, long-haired, one-eyed. He went to him, and when he returned to us we asked him: What did he say to him? He said: When I praised Allah and extolled Him and said: ""We were the furthest of people in abode, the hungriest of people, the most wretched of people, the furthest of people from every good, until Allah sent to us a Messenger, and he promised us victory in this world and Paradise in the Hereafter; we have continued to recognize from our Lord, since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, success and victory, until we came to you."""
"19231","1050 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Hayyah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped aside and I stepped aside with him; I drew near him and he said: ""Do you have water with you?"" I said: Yes. He washed his hands and face, went to wash his hands while wearing a cloak which became tight, so he brought his hand out from below the cloak, washed them, then wiped over his leather socks. Then he came to pray, while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was praying with the people; when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they cleared their throats, and he went to step back, so he signaled to him: Carry on."
"19232","Zurarah ibn Awfa and al-Hasan al-Basri from al-Mughirah. 1051 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Zurarah ibn Awfa, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind, and I stayed behind with him; he relieved himself and I brought him water for purification. He performed ablution, washed his face, intended to wash his hands - and he was wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves - so he brought his hands out from under the cloak, washed his face and forearms, wiped over the turban and the leather socks. We came to the people while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading them in the dawn prayer; when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he intended to step back, so he signaled to him to continue in his prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, I with him; when he finished his prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed another rak'ah to it, adding nothing to it."
"19233","Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani from al-Mughirah. 1052 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, (H) Abd al-Razzaq said: And Ma'mar informed me, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani: that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him a woman I was proposing to, so he said: ""Go and look at her, for it is more likely to foster affection between you."" So I came to a woman of the Ansar, proposed to her to her parents and informed them of the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it was as if they disliked that. The woman heard that while she was in her chamber, and said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you to look, then look; otherwise I adjure you - as if she deemed that grave. He said: So I looked at her and married her."" And he mentioned her compatibility."
"19234","1053 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah proposed to a woman and mentioned her matter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Have you seen her?"" He said: No. He said: ""If you are able to look at her before you marry her, do so, for it is more likely to foster affection between you."""
"19235","1054 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Sakan al-Asamm narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I proposed to a slave-girl, and when her matter drew near I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he mentioned the like of it."
"19236","1055 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I proposed to a woman and mentioned her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he mentioned the like of it."
"19237","1056 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah, he said: I proposed to a slave-girl of the Ansar and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Have you seen her?"" I said: No. He said: ""Look at her, for it is more likely to foster affection between you."""
"19238","Sa'id al-Qati'i from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 1057 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to me, Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Sa'id al-Qati'i, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make me imam of my people, so he said: ""Pray the prayer of the weakest of the people, and do not take a caller to prayer who takes a wage for his call."""
"19239","al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Aqil - and it was said al-Yashkuri - from al-Mughirah. 1058 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Aqil, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered a side (of meat) for me which was roasted; he took from my mustache upon a toothstick with a blade, trimming it with it. Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, so he threw down the blade and said to him: ""May your hands be dusted."" He said: And my mustache had grown full, so he trimmed it for me."
"19240","1059 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Mis'ar: Abu Sakhrah Jami' ibn Shaddad narrated to me, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he ordered a side (of meat) which was roasted, then took a blade and began trimming from it. Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, so he threw down the blade and said: ""What is with him, may his hands be dusted?"" He said: And my mustache had grown full, so he trimmed it upon a toothstick."
"19241","1060 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Amr al-Waki'i narrated to us: my father narrated to me, (H) and G haylan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, from Ghalib ibn Nujayh, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I took the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of a roasted side, and he was cutting with a knife. He said: ""Your mustache has grown full, O Mughirah,"" so he trimmed it upon a toothstick with the blade."
"19242","Narration of the Medinans from al-Mughirah. Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Mughirah. 1062 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out on some of his journeys - and when he went he would go far - and he commanded me to follow him with water for ablution; he came wearing a Syrian cloak, brought his hand out from under it, performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19243","1063 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went to relieve himself would go far; he went for a need while on one of his journeys and said: ""Bring me water for ablution."" So I brought him water for ablution; he brought his hands out from under the cloak, performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19244","1064 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went for a need would go far aside; he said: ""Follow me with the water."" So I followed him with a waterskin; he was wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, brought his hands out from under the cloak, performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19245","1065 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went would go far aside."
"19246","1066 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Anbasah al-Yamami narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have mentioned so-and-so woman; do you permit me to see her? He said: ""Yes; I would lie in wait for her among the date-palm trunks for her to pass by me."""
"19247","Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb from al-Mughirah. 1067 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) seeking her inheritance from her son's son or her daughter's son - I do not know which of them she was - and Abu Bakr said: I find nothing for you in the Book of Allah, and I have not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything for you; I shall ask the people this evening. When he had prayed the noon prayer he turned to the people and said: The grandmother has come to me asking me her inheritance from her son's son or her daughter's son, and I have found nothing for her in the Book, nor heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything for her; has anyone of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning her? Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah stood and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree for her a sixth. He said: Did anyone hear that with you? Muhammad ibn Maslamah stood and said: ""I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree for her a sixth."" So Abu Bakr gave her the sixth. When the caliphate of Umar came, the grandmother who opposed her came to him, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The decree was only concerning other than you; but when you are both together, the sixth is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"19248","1068 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, (H) and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Kharashah, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) asking him her inheritance in the Book of Allah, and Abu Bakr said to her: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I know nothing for you in the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); go back until I ask the people. He asked the people, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: ""I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave her the sixth."" Abu Bakr said: Is there another with you? Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughirah said, and Abu Bakr executed it for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab asking him her inheritance, and he said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the decree that was decreed was only for other than you; I shall not add anything in the shares of inheritance, but it is that sixth: if you are both together it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers. And the wording is of the hadith of Ibn Abd al-Hakam."
"19249","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 1069 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah, that he narrated from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that Umar consulted them concerning the miscarriage of a woman, and al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed in it a ghurrah. Umar said: If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that. Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree in it a ghurrah."
"19250","1070 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that Umar asked them about the miscarriage of a woman, and al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed in it a ghurrah, a slave or a slave-girl. Umar said: Who will confirm you? Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified for him."
"19251","1071 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sought their legal opinion concerning the miscarriage of a woman, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed in it a ghurrah. Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari testified for him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed it."
"19252","1072 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: ""that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to relieve himself would go far."""
"19253","1073 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he was with two men of his people, disbelievers, killed them and took their spoils; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of what he had done, and he offered him their spoils and he did not accept them."
"19254","1074 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he accompanied a people of the polytheists, found them heedless, killed them and took their wealth; he brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he disapproved of what he had done and refused to accept it."
"19255","1075 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that Umar consulted them concerning the miscarriage of a woman. Al-Mughirah said: So I said to Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed in it the ghurrah. Umar said: If you are truthful, bring me one who knows this with you. Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: ""I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree in the miscarriage of a woman the ghurrah."" So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed by it."
"19256","1076 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he accompanied a people of the polytheists, found them heedless and killed them, took their wealth and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to accept it."
"19257","Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi from al-Mughirah. 1077 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from al-Mughirah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a standing and informed us of what will be in his ummah until the Day of Resurrection; whoever retained it retained it, and whoever forgot it forgot it."
"19258","Abu al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, from al-Mughirah. 1078 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us: Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir informed me: Abu al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah al-Taymi, informed me that he heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a journey, dismounted at a stop and went aside; I followed him with a waterskin. When he came I met him, poured for him, he performed ablution wearing leather socks, wiped over them, then prayed the dawn prayer."
"19259","1079 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Abi al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19260","1080 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us: Sharik ibn Abi Namir narrated to me, from Abi al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey - and al-Mughirah was on that journey - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went one day for his need, and I followed his tracks with a waterskin of water; I cleared the way for him, and he performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19261","1081 - Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ansanawi al-Misri narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Salim informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abi al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."""
"19262","Abu Mus'ab al-Makki from al-Mughirah. 1082 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, (H) and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, they said: Awn ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Mus'ab al-Makki, he said: I met Anas ibn Malik and Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and I heard them narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah commanded a tree on the night of the cave, and it grew in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Allah commanded the spider and it wove in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); He commanded two wild pigeons and they stood at the mouth of the cave. The youths of Quraysh came - a man from every clan - with their sticks, clubs and swords, until when they were forty cubits from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them hastened to look into the cave and saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so he returned to his companions. They said to him: Why did you not look into the cave? He said: I saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so I knew there was no one in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard what he said and knew that Allah had warded off from him by means of them, so he supplicated for them, invoked blessing upon them, prescribed their recompense and they were settled in the sanctuary."""
"19263","Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from al-Mughirah. 1083 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I sought permission to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Makkah and Madinah. He said: ""Come to me tonight at Harada."" And I did not prefer anything over him until morning."
"19264","Hunaydah al-Ta'ifi from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 1084 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sirrar al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Abi Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yunus ibn al-Harith al-Ta'ifi narrated to us: Hunaydah narrated to me, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says upon me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"19265","1085 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, they said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, (H) and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us: that he heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani saying: I asked al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah about what he witnessed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Tabuk, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the campaign of Tabuk and wiped over his leather socks."
"19266","Those named Ma'mar. Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadlah al-Adawi al-Qurashi - and he is Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadlah ibn Harthan ibn Awf ibn Ubayd ibn Uwayj ibn Adi ibn Ka'b - and his mother was Ash'ari; he was among the emigrants to Abyssinia who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two ships. 1086 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadlah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever hoards is a sinner."""
"19267","1087 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadlah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None hoards but a sinner."" Muhammad said: And Sa'id used to hoard, and Ma'mar used to hoard."
"19268","1088 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Rishdin, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Alqamah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""None hoards but a sinner."""
"19269","1089 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadlah ibn Adi ibn Ka'b: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None hoards but a sinner."" So I said to Sa'id: You hoard. He said: Ma'mar used to hoard."
"19270","1090 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hatim and Bazi' ibn Farid narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from Qudamah ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ata, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""None hoards but a sinner."""
"19271","1091 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None hoards but a sinner."""
"19272","1092 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar, from a man of Quraysh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None hoards but a sinner."""
"19273","1093 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Maryam: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to announce among the people at Mina: ""The days of tashriq are days of eating and drinking."""
"19274","1094 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abi al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Food for food: like for like."""
"19275","1095 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abi al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi: that he sent a slave-boy of his with a sa' and said: Sell it, then buy barley with it. The boy went and took a sa' plus part of a sa'. When Ma'mar came he informed him of that, and Ma'mar said: Why did you do so? Go and return it; take only like for like, for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Food like for like."" And our food in those days was barley. It was said: It is not like it. He said: I fear it resembles usury."
"19276","1096 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, he said: I heard my father, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq saying: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah, he said: I heard Ma'mar saying: I used to saddle for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Ma'mar, tonight I found looseness in my saddle straps."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had tied them as I used to tie them, but one who envies me for that wanted to replace me. He said: ""I shall indeed not do that."" When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished his pilgrimage, he commanded me and I took the razor and sharpened it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Ma'mar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has enabled you to the lobe of his ear, with the razor in your hand."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I deem that a favor upon me and a grace. He said: ""Yes."" He said: So add to that."
"19277","1 - ... So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did you grant all your sons?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then take it back."""
"19278","2 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Isa al-Tahhan Musa, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father or his brother - from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Those who mention Allah's majesty; His glorification, His magnification and His praise - circle around the Throne; they have a humming like the humming of bees, mentioning their companion. Does not one of you love that there ever remain with the Most Merciful those mentioning him?"""
"19279","3 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muslim, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from his father or his brother - from al-Nu'man, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who mention Allah's majesty; His glorification, His praise, His magnification and His declaring His oneness - incline around the Throne; they have a humming like the humming of bees, mentioning their companion. Does not one of you love that there ever remain with the Most Merciful those mentioning him?"""
"19280","4 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah: that al-Dahhak ibn Qays asked al-Nu'man ibn Bashir: What would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite after Surah al-Jumu'ah? He said: ""Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?"""
"19281","5 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah: that al-Dahhak ibn Qays wrote to al-Nu'man ibn Bashir asking him: What would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite on Friday along with Surah al-Jumu'ah? He said: ""Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?"""
"19282","6 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters most people do not know. Whoever avoids doubtful matters clears his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into doubtful matters falls into the unlawful - like one grazing around a sanctuary, about to enter it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions."""
"19283","7 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... and he mentioned the like of it."
"19284","8 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari and Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shu'aythi narrated to us, they said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between that are doubtful matters - and perhaps he said: ambiguous - and I shall strike for you a parable concerning that: Allah has set a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is what He prohibited; whoever grazes around the sanctuary is about to mix with doubt, and whoever mixes with doubt is about to dare."""
"19285","9 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Khaythamah and al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Lawful is clear and unlawful is clear, and doubts between that; whoever leaves doubtful matters is more likely to leave the unlawful. The prohibitions of Allah are a sanctuary, so whoever grazes around the sanctuary is near to grazing in it."""
"19286","10 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Farwah al-Hamdani, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - with the like of it."
"19287","11 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Farwah al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir on the minbar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there are doubtful matters between them. Whoever leaves what appears doubtful to him of sin will be more ready to leave what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts about will soon fall into the unlawful. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on the earth is His acts of disobedience."""
"19288","12 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Khaybari al-Lakhmi, the two Damascenes, narrated to us, they said: Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to me, he said: Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between the lawful and the unlawful are doubtful matters; many people do not know whether they are of the lawful or of the unlawful. Whenever a man leaves them he is more careful in clearing his honor and his religion, and whenever he falls into them he will soon fall into the unlawful - like one who grazes beside the sanctuary and will soon graze within the sanctuary. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19289","13 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi and Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi narrated to us, they said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Warqa' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similar to it."
"19290","14 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; many people do not know whether they are of the lawful or of the unlawful. Whoever leaves them will have cleared his honor, and whoever falls into any of them will soon fall into the unlawful - just as whoever grazes around the sanctuary will soon fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19291","15 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there are doubtful matters between them. Whoever leaves what appears doubtful to him of sin will be more ready to leave what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts about will soon fall into the sanctuary - like one who grazes beside the sanctuary and will soon fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on the earth is His acts of disobedience."""
"19292","16 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr al-Ahwal narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us. (H) And al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us; both of them from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid, from Amir; that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between the lawful and the unlawful are doubtful matters. Whoever leaves them safeguards his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them will soon fall into the unlawful - like one who grazes close to the sanctuary and will soon graze within it. Every king has a sanctuary on the earth, and the sanctuary of Allah on the earth is His sacred prohibitions."" And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Malik al-Janbi."
"19293","17 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters..."" and he mentioned the hadith."
"19294","18 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between the lawful and the unlawful are doubts. Whoever leaves them clears himself for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them will soon fall into the unlawful - like one who grazes beside the sanctuary and will soon graze within it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is that which He has declared protected for His servants."""
"19295","19 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir informed us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His lawful and His unlawful, and doubtful matters are between them - just as if a shepherd were beside the sanctuary, his sheep would soon graze within it. So avoid doubtful matters."""
"19296","20 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My uncle Sa'id ibn Isa ibn Talid al-Ru'ayni narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Ukli and Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hamdani, from Amir al-Sha'bi; that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Place between yourselves and the unlawful a barrier of the lawful; whoever does that will be more careful in clearing his honor and his religion, and whoever grazes within it will be like one who grazes beside the sanctuary and will soon fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on the earth is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19297","21 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarah, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressed us and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear. Whoever leaves doubtful matters is more ready to leave sacred prohibitions, and whoever ventures to enter the sanctuary will fall into the sanctuary."""
"19298","22 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir ibn Ibrahim al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Ya'qub al-Qummi, from Harun ibn Antarah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19299","23 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri and Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Madini narrated to us. And Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me; they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters..."" the hadith."
"19300","24 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O people! Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on the earth is His lawful and His unlawful, and doubtful matters are between them. If a shepherd grazed around the edges of a sanctuary, his sheep would soon graze in its middle - so leave doubtful matters."""
"19301","25 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Aflah ibn Sa'id, from Imran ibn Dinar, from Malih ibn Abdullah al-Khathmi, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Behold, the lawful is clear, and behold, the unlawful is clear, and behold, between them are doubtful matters which many people do not know. Whoever avoids doubtful matters will have cleared himself for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into doubtful matters will fall into the unlawful - like a shepherd around the sanctuary who will soon graze within it. Behold, every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19302","26 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Asad al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there is doubt in between. Whoever leaves what makes him doubt for what does not make him doubt will be more ready to leave what is clear to him, and whoever leaves what does not make him doubt will soon ride into what makes him doubt. Behold, every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His acts of disobedience, and whoever grazes around the sanctuary will soon graze within the sanctuary."""
"19303","27 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Shu'ayb al-Kaysani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Rassasi narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir - Abd al-Malik said: And I heard it from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever leaves them, that will be a clearing for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them will soon fall into the unlawful."""
"19304","28 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of one who upholds the limits of Allah and one who falls into them is like the parable of people who drew lots on a ship: some of them got its upper part and some got its lower part. They said: If only we made a hole in our share and drew water from it, and did not harm those above us! If they leave them to what they want, they will all perish, and if they restrain them, they will all be saved."""
"19305","29 - al-Abbas al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: I heard on this minbar - meaning the minbar of Kufah - a man saying from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I never heard a man say before him. Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind said to him: Who is he, O Amir? He said: He is al-Nu'man ibn Bashir al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of one who is lenient in the matter of Allah is like the parable of a group who boarded a ship and drew lots for dwellings in it: some got the upper part of the ship and some got its lower part. One looking from the upper part of the ship looked down, and there was one of those in the lower part boring a hole in it. He said to him: What are you doing, O so-and-so? He said: I am making a hole to draw water from it and perform ablution and drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they change his course he will be saved and they will be saved by the permission of Allah, and if they leave him boring it he will drown and they will drown."""
"19306","30 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'ah, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19307","31 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of one who upholds the limits of Allah and one who is lenient in them is like the parable of people who drew lots on a ship at sea: some got its upper part and some got its lower part. Those in the lower part would go out and draw water and pour it over those in the upper part, and they harmed them; so they stopped them. They said: We will not let you pass by us and harm us. Those in the lower part said: Since you have stopped us, we shall bore through the ship and draw water. If they restrain them and stop them, they will all be saved, and if they leave them, they will all perish."""
"19308","32 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of one who upholds the limits of Allah is the parable of people who boarded a ship and drew lots for its dwellings: the place of filth and the pouring of water and the passage of the people fell to one of them, so he became annoyed, took an adze and began boring in the ship. One of them said to the other: Do you want to drown us and drown their ship? The other said: Leave him; he is only boring through his own place!"""
"19309","33 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19310","34 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""One who is lenient in the limits of Allah, and one who rides over the limits of Allah, and one who enjoins them and forbids their violation - are like the parable of people who drew lots on one of the ships of the sea: some got the rear of the ship, farthest from the facility, and they were foolish. Whenever they passed by the baggage of the people they harmed them, so they said: We are the nearest people of the ship to the facility and the farthest from the sky; between us and the facility is that we bore through the ship, then we shall block it when we no longer need it. Their foolish counterparts said: Do it. So he reached for an axe and struck the side of the ship with it. A man looked over him and adjured him, he said: What are you doing? He said: We are nearest to you to the facility and farthest from it; I shall bore through the hull of this ship, and when we no longer need it we shall block it. He said: Do not do it; for then you will perish and we shall perish."""
"19311","35 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""The parable of one who upholds the limits of Allah, and one who falls into them, and one who is lenient in them, is the parable of a group who drew lots on a ship: some got its upper part, some got its lower part, and some got its middle. Whenever one wanted to draw water he passed by those above him and they were harmed by him. When they saw that, he took the axe and said: I shall bore here and draw water from nearby. Those above him said: Do not do it; do you want to destroy us?! The other said: Woe to him! He is only acting in his own share. If they restrain him they will be saved and he will be saved, and if they do not, he will perish and they will perish."""
"19312","36 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of one who is lenient in the limits, and one who falls into them, and one who upholds them, is like the parable of three men who boarded a ship and drew lots for their dwellings: one of them got its lowest, roughest and worst part, another got its middle, and another got its upper part. His passage and the pouring of his water was upon them, and they did not warn him until he wanted to make a hole in it, saying: It is nearer to the water, and there will be no passing by you. Some of them said: Leave him - may Allah banish him! He is only boring through his own share. And the other said: Do not leave him; he will only destroy us. If they restrain him they will be safe, and if they leave him they will perish."""
"19313","37 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Ajlah, from Amir, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir on the minbar at Kufah saying: O people, restrain your fools; for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A people boarded a ship at sea and drew lots, and every man took his share. One of them took an axe and began boring through his share. They said: What are you doing? If you do it, we shall drown and you will drown. If they do not restrain him, they will drown and he will drown, and if they restrain him, he will be saved and they will be saved."""
"19314","38 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Amir al-Sha'bi; that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of the sinner among the people is like the parable of people who boarded a ship at sea and divided it, so every one of them got a place. One man set out to his place and bored through it. They said to him: What do you want?! Do you want to destroy us?! He said: And what business is it of yours with my place?! If they leave him, they will drown and he will drown with them, and if they restrain him, they will be saved and he will be saved; that is the parable of the sinner."""
"19315","39 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers in their mutual mercy, love and affection is like the parable of the body: if one limb of it complains, the rest of the body responds with fever and sleeplessness."""
"19316","40 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of the believers, the parable of their love and mutual affection, is the parable of the body: when it complains, the rest of it responds with fever and ailments."""
"19317","41 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believers are like one man: if his head complains, the rest of the body responds to it with fever and sleeplessness."""
"19318","42 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H) And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believer is like the parable of the body: when his head complains, the rest of his body responds."""
"19319","43 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath and al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers in their love, mutual giving and mutual mercy is the parable of the body: when anything of it complains, the rest of the body responds to it."""
"19320","44 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19321","45 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19322","46 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of the believers in their mutual mercy and the kindness of one another is like the body of a man: when part of his body complains, the rest of his body feels pain for it."""
"19323","47 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir informed us. And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The believers ought to be among themselves - in their mutual mercy of one another and the sincere advice of one another - like the parable of the body: when a limb of it complains and responds, his whole body responds with sleeplessness until the pain of that limb departs."""
"19324","48 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The believers ought to be among themselves like the standing of one man: when a limb of his body complains, the rest of his body responds."""
"19325","49 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Sha'bi, al-Nu'man ibn Bashir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers is only like the body: when anything complains, the rest of the body responds to it."""
"19326","50 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, while on the minbar, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The believers are like the parable of a man: when anything of his body aches, the rest of his body responds to it."""
"19327","51 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us. (H) And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, both from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people, show mercy to one another; the Muslims are like one man: when a limb of him complains, the rest of his body responds for it."""
"19328","52 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers is like the parable of one body: when part of it complains, all of it responds with sleeplessness and pain."""
"19329","53 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Behold, in the body there is a morsel: when it is sound the whole body is sound, and when it is corrupt the whole body is corrupt; behold, it is the heart."""
"19330","54 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In the son of Adam there is a morsel: when it is sound it is sound, and when it is corrupt it is corrupt: the heart."""
"19331","55 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19332","56 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19333","57 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Of the son of Adam there is a morsel: when it is sound, the body is sound for it, and when it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt: the heart."""
"19334","58 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Talib narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""In the body there is a morsel: when it is sound, such-and-such is sound for it, and the rest of his body."""
"19335","59 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""In the body there is a morsel: when it is sound the whole body is sound, and when it is corrupt the whole body is corrupt."""
"19336","60 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Ash'ath, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""In the body there is a morsel: when it is sound the whole body is sound, and when it is corrupt the body is corrupt, and it is the heart."""
"19337","61 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""In the body there is a morsel: when it is safe the body is safe; behold, it is the heart."""
"19338","62 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Sha'bi, al-Nu'man ibn Bashir said on this minbar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In man there is a morsel: when it is sound the whole body is sound, and when it ails, the rest of the body ails for it; behold, it is the heart."""
"19339","63 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""In the body there is a morsel: when it is safe the whole body is safe, and when it ails the whole body ails; behold, it is the heart."""
"19340","64 - Abdan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My ear heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""In man there is a morsel: when it is sound his body is sound, and when it ails, the rest of his body ails for it."""
"19341","65 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My mother Amrah bint Rawahah said to my father: If only you would grant al-Nu'man a gift or give to him, and call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness it! So he granted me, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you given all your children the like of what you have given him?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then do not call me to witness injustice; for your sons have a right upon you that you be just to them, just as you have upon them that they be dutiful to you."""
"19342","66 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from al-Sha'bi, that the mother of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir said to his father: Grant him, and call the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you granted all of them?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then would you call me to witness injustice?! They have a right upon you that you be just among them, and you have upon them a right that they be dutiful to you."""
"19343","67 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, Amir narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: My father Bashir gave me a gift, and my mother said: Call the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness it. So he took my hand and we set out until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Messenger of Allah! The mother of this boy asked me to give him a gift, so I gave it to him, and she said: Call the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness it, so I have come to you to call you to witness. He said: ""Slowly! Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them what you have given this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then do not call me to witness injustice. Your sons have a right upon you that you be just among them, and you have upon them a right that they be dutiful to you."" So he returned and did not give it to me."
"19344","68 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father gave me charity, and my mother Amrah bint Rawahah said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. So my father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son from Amrah - I have given him charity, and she said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Slowly! Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them the like of what you have given him?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then fear Allah and be just among them, just as you have upon them a right that they be dutiful to you."""
"19345","69 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us. (H) And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir on this minbar of ours saying: Amrah bint Rawahah asked Bashir ibn Sa'd to grant me a gift from his wealth, and he refused her. Then it occurred to him after a year or two to grant it to me, and he said to her: What you asked for your son - I had withheld it, and it has occurred to me to grant it to him. And she said: I shall not be pleased until you take him by the hand and go with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and call him to witness. So he took my hand and set out with me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Prophet of Allah, Amrah bint Rawahah asked me to grant this son of mine a gift, and I had refused her, then it occurred to me to grant it to him, and she said: I shall not be pleased until you take him by the hand and go with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and call him to witness. He said: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given every one of them what you have given this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then I shall not witness to this; this is injustice. Call someone else than me to witness to this. Be just among your children in gifts, just as you love that they be just among you in dutifulness and kindness."" And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi'."
"19346","70 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Miqsam narrated to me, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - and I thought I never heard a man after him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Amrah bint Rawahah - she is the mother of al-Nu'man - wanted him to grant me a gift, and he withheld it for a year, then it occurred to him to give me. She said: I shall not be pleased until you take my son by the hand and bring him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he took my hand and brought me to him, and mentioned that to him. He said: Then do not call me to witness to this. Al-Mughirah said: I do not know whether he said: 'injustice' or said: 'compulsion.' Then he said: Be just among your children in gifts, just as you love that they be just among you in dutifulness and kindness."""
"19347","71 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar, Mughirah, Dawud ibn Abi Hind, Isma'il ibn Salim and Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father granted me a gift - Isma'il said: He granted him a slave boy - and my mother Amrah bint Rawahah said to him: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and call him to witness. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and said: I have granted my son al-Nu'man a gift, and Amrah asked me to call you to witness to that. He said: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them the like of what you have given al-Nu'man?"" He said: No. Some of these narrators said: ""This is injustice,"" and some of them said: ""This is compulsion; call someone else than me to witness to this."" Al-Mughirah said: ""Does it not please you that they be equal to you in kindness and dutifulness?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then call someone else than me to witness to this."" And Mujalid mentioned in his hadith: ""They have a right upon you that you be just among them, just as you have upon them a right that they be dutiful to you."""
"19348","72 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; that his father gave him charity, and his mother said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have given my son charity, and his mother asked me to call you to witness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them?"" He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be just among them."""
"19349","73 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli Abu Mu'adh narrated to us, from Abu Hariz. (H) And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz, from al-Sha'bi; that he narrated to him that al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressed at Kufah and said: My father Bashir ibn Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Amrah bint Rawahah has given birth to a boy, and I have named him al-Nu'man, and she has refused to raise him until I assign to him a garden of mine - the best wealth I own - and she said: Call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness to that. He said: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Do not call me to witness except to justice; for I do not witness to injustice."" And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Muqaddami. And the name of Abu Hariz is Abdullah ibn Husayn, judge of Sijistan."
"19350","74 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara' narrated to us, he said: Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; that Bashir ibn Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Amrah bint Rawahah wanted me to give her son charity, and she ordered me to call you to witness to that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you have any sons besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them as you have given this one?"" He said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then do not call me to witness to injustice."""
"19351","75 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, they said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: My father gave me a gift, and my mother Amrah bint Rawahah said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have given my son from Amrah a gift, and she ordered me to call you to witness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you given all your children the like of this?"" He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then be just among your children."" So he returned and took back his gift."
"19352","76 - al-Nu'man ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Dawud, Husayn, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani and Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from al-Sha'bi, and from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: We heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir while he was addressing on the minbar, he said: My father gave me charity, and Amrah bint Rawahah - she is the mother of al-Nu'man - said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness to it. So Bashir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have given my son charity, and Amrah bint Rawahah - she is the mother of al-Nu'man - said: I shall not be pleased until you call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness to it. He said: ""Do you have any sons besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them the like of what you have given this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""This is injustice; then do not call me to witness to it. Fear Allah and be just among your children just as you love that they be dutiful to you."" He said: So my father took back his charity."
"19353","77 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""Allah loves that you be just among your children."""
"19354","78 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr and Yahya ibn Mu'adh al-Tustariyyan narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Adami narrated to us, they said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father took my hand and went with me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: This is my son, and his mother has asked me to grant him from my wealth and to call you to witness to it. He said: ""Do you have any child besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you assigned to all of them the like of what you have assigned to this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""Would you have me witness to injustice?!"" He said: So we returned as we had gone."
"19355","79 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, that Nu'man ibn Bashir - his mother said: O Bashir, grant al-Nu'man. She kept pressing him until he granted him, and she said: Call the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness to it. So he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the testimony to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Have you granted your sons the like of that?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then I do not witness to injustice."" Awn said to me: And as for me, I heard my father saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then make them equal."""
"19356","80 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-Askari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to me, from Mughirah and Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his father: ""Do not call me to witness to injustice."""
"19357","81 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father granted me a gift, and she said to my father: Call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to call him to witness, and he said: ""Call someone else than me to witness to this."""
"19358","82 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to call him to witness to a gift he was giving me. He said: ""Do you have any besides him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Have you given all of them the like of what you have given this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then I do not witness to injustice."""
"19359","83 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it, except that he said: ""I do not witness to deviation."""
"19360","84 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""He does not thank Allah who does not thank people; speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude; unity is mercy, and division is torment."""
"19361","85 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated to me, Abu Waki' narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid Abu Abd al-Rahman, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""He does not thank Allah who does not thank people; speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude; unity is mercy, and division is torment."""
"19362","86 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Of wheat there is wine, and of barley there is wine, and of dates there is wine, and of honey there is wine."""
"19363","87 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""Of wheat there is wine, and of barley there is wine, and of raisins there is wine, and of honey there is wine."""
"19364","88 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Of wheat there is wine, and of barley there is wine, and of honey there is wine, and of dates there is wine, and of raisins there is wine."""
"19365","89 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""Of wheat there is wine, and of barley there is wine, and of honey there is wine, and of raisins there is wine."""
"19366","90 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us. (H) And al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani narrated to him, that al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to him, that al-Sha'bi narrated to him; that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Of wheat there is wine, and of raisins there is wine, and of dates there is wine, and of honey there is wine. And I forbid every intoxicant."""
"19367","91 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Jarir ibn al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Avoid every intoxicant."""
"19368","92 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O people! Of grapes there is wine, and of dates there is wine, and of wheat there is wine, and of barley there is wine, and of honey there is wine, and I forbid every intoxicant."""
"19369","93 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz; that Amir narrated to him that al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressed the people at Kufah and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Wine is from juice, raisins, dates, wheat, barley and corn, and I forbid you every intoxicant."""
"19370","94 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi and Mujahid, they said: al-Nu'man ibn Bashir came to us and addressed us, and said in his address: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us in Masjid al-Khayf and said: ""May Allah brighten the face of a servant who hears my saying and conveys it; many a carrier of understanding is not understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of a believer does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to those in authority, and sticking to the community of the Muslims; for their supplication encompasses those behind them."""
"19371","95 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us; they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Restrain your fools."""
"19372","96 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah and al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths will precede their testimony, and whose testimony will precede their oaths."""
"19373","97 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abdullah, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever ties an animal on the road of the Muslims and it injures, he is liable."""
"19374","98 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my uncle Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressed us. (H) And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sufyan al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, from Simak ibn Harb, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; while he was addressing on the minbar of Kufah - and most of what he narrated to us on his minbar - he said: ""Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than a man who loaded his provisions and his water-skin on a camel, then set out traveling, until when he was in a desert land the midday rest overtook him and he alighted, and lay down under a tree, and his eyes overcame him, and his camel slipped away. He woke up startled, then climbed an elevation and looked and saw nothing, then climbed another elevation and looked and saw nothing, then climbed a third elevation and looked and saw nothing, then came to the place where he had lain and sat in it. While he was sitting, having come close to destruction, his camel walked until it placed its halter in his hand. Allah is more joyful at the repentance of the servant than he was when he found his camel in that state."" He said: So Simak claimed that al-Sha'bi or al-Lakhmi - Simak does not know which of them it is - that al-Nu'man ibn Bashir raised it that day to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abi Adi. And Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh said in his hadith: Simak said: Al-Sha'bi claimed that al-Nu'man raised this hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and as for me, I did not hear it. And he did not mention al-Lakhmi. And al-Lakhmi is Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr."
"19375","99 - Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Sayf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not drink in naqir nor in muzaffat."""
"19376","100 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths will precede their testimony, and whose testimony will precede their oaths."""
"19377","101 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of this ummah is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will spread a people whose oaths will precede their testimonies, and whose testimonies will precede their oaths."""
"19378","102 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths will precede their testimony, and whose testimony will precede their oaths."""
"19379","103 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony will precede their oaths, and whose oaths will precede their testimony."""
"19380","104 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths will precede their testimony, and whose testimony will precede their oaths."""
"19381","105 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19382","106 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Muslims are like one man: when his eye complains, all of him complains, and when his head complains, all of him complains."""
"19383","107 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it."
"19384","108 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard A'ishah raising her voice to him. He said: O daughter of Umm Ruman, do you raise your voice to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! So he reached for her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came between him and her. Then Abu Bakr went out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept pleasing her: ""Did you not see me come between the man and you?!"" Then he came another time seeking permission and heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughing with her. He sought permission, and Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, include me in your peace as you included me in your war!"
"19385","109 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was A'ishah raising her voice to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O daughter of so-and-so, do you raise your voice to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came between him and her. Then Abu Bakr went out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began pleasing her, and said: ""Did you not see me come between the man and you?!"" Then Abu Bakr sought permission another time, and heard him laughing with her. Abu Bakr said: Include me in your peace as you included me in your war!"
"19386","110 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was A'ishah, and she was saying: By Allah, I know he is dearer to you than my father - meaning Ali. Abu Bakr raised his voice to her and said: I do not see you but raising your voice to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Then he entered to her after that while she was laughing with him, and said: Include me in your peace as you included me in your war!"
"19387","111 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me. (H) And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""You shall straighten your rows in your prayer, or Allah shall surely set your hearts at variance!"""
"19388","112 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten us in the rows as he straightens the arrow with us; he would do that with us repeatedly, until when he saw that we had learned, he stepped forward. Then he saw the chest of a man protruding, and said: ""O servants of Allah, the Muslims! You shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance."""
"19389","113 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us. (H) And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, they said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our rows in prayer as he straightens arrows or spears."
"19390","114 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us; Simak ibn Harb informed me, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressing, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten the rows until they were like the spear or arrows. Then he saw the chest of a man protruding and said: ""O servants of Allah: straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19391","115 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten the rows until it was as if he straightened arrows with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until when he was about to say takbir he saw a man with his chest sticking out from the row, and said: ""O servants of Allah, you shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19392","116 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb informed us, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten us in prayer as arrows are straightened, until when he thought we had taken that from him and understood it; then one day he turned to us with his face and there was a man standing out with his chest. He said: ""You shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19393","117 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our rows as if he straightened arrows with them, until he saw that we had understood from him. Then one day he came out and stood until he was about to say takbir, and saw a man with his chest out of the row. He said: ""O servants of Allah, you shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19394","118 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Hinna'i narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressing while he was over Kufah - and he was among the most eloquent of people - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our rows, and when they were even he would say takbir. He would straighten our rows until when he thought we had become even, a glance came from him, and there was a man in front of the row. He said: ""You shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19395","119 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten the rows in prayer as arrows are straightened."
"19396","120 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he would straighten the rows as arrows are straightened - and he saw the chest of a man out of the row, and said: ""You shall straighten your chests, or Allah shall surely set your faces at variance!"""
"19397","121 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Allah, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of the servant than a man who was on a journey, with a riding animal carrying his goods, provisions, food and drink. He alighted in the shade of a tree and tied his riding animal, and sleep overcame him. He woke up and his riding animal had gone. He stood and sought it, and climbed an elevation and saw nothing, then climbed an elevation and saw nothing. He said: By Allah, I shall return to the place where I was and take the midday rest in it until I die. So he returned and slept, then woke up, and raised his head, and there was his riding animal dragging its halter. Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than that one was at his camel."""
"19398","122 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressing, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire!"" - until if a man were in the market he would have heard him from this station of mine, until a khamisah that was on his shoulder fell at his feet."
"19399","123 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H) And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. (H) And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, while on the minbar of Kufah, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while on the minbar, saying: ""O people! I warn you of the Fire!"" - until if he were in this place of mine the people of the market would have heard, or whomsoever Allah willed to hear."
"19400","124 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the minbar: ""I warn you of the Fire!"" - until if anyone were in the farthest part of the market he would have heard him."
"19401","125 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the last Isha."
"19402","126 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill of daqal, and you are not content with less than varieties of dates, butter and varieties of clothes!"
"19403","127 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, and he mentioned what people had attained of the world, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spend the day and find no food to fill his stomach!"
"19404","128 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H) And Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, saying: ""Are you not in food and drink as you wish? I saw your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finding no daqal to fill his stomach."""
"19405","129 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Muhammad ibn Hisab narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard him on the minbar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not find daqal to fill his stomach from hunger."
"19406","130 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believers are like the body: when part of it complains, the rest of it responds."""
"19407","131 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of the believers is the parable of one man: when anything of his body complains, the rest of it responds to it."""
"19408","132 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, concerning His saying: {And do not throw yourselves with your hands into destruction}: He said: A man would commit a sin and say: I shall not be forgiven. So Allah revealed: {And do not throw yourselves with your hands into destruction, and do good; indeed Allah loves the doers of good}."
"19409","133 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah and His angels bless the first row"" - or he said: ""the first rows."""
"19410","134 - And with his isnad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever grants a loan of silver or gold, or gives milk to drink, or guides through an alley, it is equal to freeing a neck."""
"19411","135 - Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, Affan ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a man dozed off on his mount. A man took an arrow from his quiver, and the man woke up frightened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a man to frighten a Muslim."""
"19412","136 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Husayn Abu Malik al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {By the sun and its brightness}."
"19413","137 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the mujahid in the path of Allah is the parable of one who fasts by day and stands by night until he returns, whenever he returns."""
"19414","138 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fear the Fire, even with half a date."""
"19415","139 - Abdan ibn Ahmad, Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani and al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, they said: Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah hears him who praises Him,"" none of us would bend his back until he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating."
"19416","140 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhallab ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Bayan al-Saffar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Simak ibn Harb saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The parable of the rulers and the parable of the people is like the parable of people who boarded a ship: one of them wanted to bore through it. If they restrain him, he will be saved and they will be saved, and if they leave him, he will perish and they will perish."""
"19417","141 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhallab ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Bayan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Simak saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Be upright to Quraysh as long as they are upright to you. If they are not upright to you, then place your swords on your shoulders and annihilate their multitude."""
"19418","142 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us. (H) And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, they said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""There is no servant nor maidservant but he has three friends: a friend who says: I am with you, so take from me what you wish; that is his wealth. And a friend who says: I am with you, but when you come to the door of the king I shall leave you; those are his servants and his family. And a friend who says: I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you go out; that is his deed."""
"19419","143 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir - the like of it, and he did not raise it."
"19420","144 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; the like of it, and he did not raise it."
"19421","145 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud al-Zajjaj narrated to us, Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three men set out...."" and he mentioned the hadith."
"19422","146 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Za'faranî narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Tara'ifi al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""Three men set out seeking provision for their families, and rain befell them, so they took refuge in a cave, and a leaning rock fell upon them so that they saw no opening from it. One of them said to another: The rock has fallen, and the trace has been effaced, and none knows your place here but Allah, so let each one of you supplicate by his best deed. A man among them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel, then bring it to them; and when I found them sleeping I feared to wake them lest drowsiness increase in their heads, while my children were saying: Give us to drink, give us to drink. And I kept standing until they woke up. O Allah, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your torment, then relieve us. So the rock moved. And the other said: O Allah, if You know that my father left wealth, and that my brother...."" and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"19423","147 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: ""In man there is a morsel: when it is sound the rest of the body is sound, and when it is corrupt the rest of the body is corrupt; and it is the heart."""
"19424","148 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Before the Hour there will be liars."""
"19425","149 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nayzak narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him privately, and he said: ""Tell them to kill him."" When the man had gone, he said: ""Bring him to me."" Then he said: ""Does he perhaps say: There is no god but Allah?!"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then do not kill him, for I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."""
"19426","150 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Asadi narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers in their love and mutual mercy is like the parable of the body: when part of it complains, all of it responds with sleeplessness and fever."""
"19427","151 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of the believers in their mutual connection, mutual mercy and what Allah has placed among them is like the parable of the body: when part of it aches, all of it aches with sleeplessness and fever."""
"19428","152 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Bustanban narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Bashir addressed us and said: ""Allah has made a clear lawful and a clear unlawful, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever leaves them has cleared himself for his religion and his honor, and whoever rides into them will soon fall into the unlawful."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a parable for us and said: ""Whoever grazes around the sanctuary will soon fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19429","153 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Sinan al-Nahartiri narrated to us, Umar ibn Shabib al-Musalli narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr - Abu Hafs said: And I heard it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr - from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever leaves them will be more careful in clearing his honor and his religion, and whoever rides into them will soon ride into the unlawful - like one who grazes beside the sanctuary and will soon graze within it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His sacred prohibitions."""
"19430","154 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The lightest of the people of the Fire in torment on the Day of Resurrection will be a man with two coals in the hollows of his feet, from which his brain will boil as the pot or the ewer boils."""
"19431","Haddathana Daran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan al-Basri, thana 'Amr ibn Marzuq, thana Shu'ba, 'an Abi Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment will be one who has two embers in the hollows of his feet, from which his brain boils."""
"19432","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Abu Usama, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment on the Day of Resurrection will be one who has two sandals and two straps of Fire, his brain boiling from them as a cauldron boils; he will not think that anyone among the people of the Fire suffers a punishment more severe than his, yet he is the lightest of them in punishment."""
"19433","Haddathana al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Fasawi, thana Nasr ibn al-Harish al-Samit, thana Rawh ibn Musafir, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment on the Day of Resurrection is a man who has two sandals of Fire, from which his brain boils."""
"19434","Haddathana Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, thana Tamim ibn al-Muntasir, thana Ishaq al-Azraq, 'an Sharik, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Indeed, the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man who has two sandals of Fire, from which his brain boils."""
"19435","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdous ibn Kamil, thana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr, thana Muhammad ibn Abi 'Ubayda, thana my father, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Amr ibn Shurahbil, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There were three men walking in the aftermath of rain when they passed by a cave, and they said: If only you would take shelter in this cave. So they took shelter in it, and while they were inside, a rock fell from the mountain, of that which descends out of fear of Allah, until it blocked the cave. Then some of them said to others: You will find nothing better than for each one of you to supplicate by means of the best deed he ever did. One of them said: O Allah, I was a farmer and I had hired laborers, and among them was a man who did the work of two men, so I gave him his wage just as I gave the laborers, but he said: I do the work of two men and you give me the wage of one man?! So he left in anger and abandoned his wage with me, and I sowed it in its own plot, and it multiplied, then I sowed it again and it multiplied, until the grain became many heaps. Then the man became needy and came to me asking for his wage, so I said: Go to those heaps, for they are your wage. He said: Are you wronging me and mocking me?! I said: I am not mocking you. So he went and took it. O Allah, if You know that I did that out of fear of You and seeking Your Face, then uncover it from us. Then the rock said: Qid! And they saw the light. Then the second one said: O Allah, I courted a woman for herself and gave her one hundred dinars, and when she gave me access to herself she wept, so I said: What makes you weep? She said: I did this out of need! So I said: Go, and the hundred is yours. And I left her. O Allah, if You know that I did that only out of fear of You and seeking Your Face, then uncover it from us. Then the rock said: Qid! And a great opening split open in it. Then the other one said: O Allah, I had two elderly parents, and I had sheep, and I used to bring them milk every night, but one night I was delayed from them until they slept, so I came and found them asleep, and I disliked waking them, and I disliked going away lest they wake up, so I stood with the vessel over their heads until morning. O Allah, if You know that I did that only out of fear of You and seeking Your Face, then uncover it. Then the rock said: Qid! And it was uncovered from them, and they walked out."""
"19436","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdous ibn Kamil, thana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr, thana Ishaq ibn Sulayman, thana Abu Sinan, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, the like of it."
"19437","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa, anba Isra'il, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an a man of Bajila, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, three men set out on a journey..."" and he mentioned the like of it."
"19438","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, 'an 'Abd al-Razzaq, 'an al-Thawri, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids and on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}."
"19439","Haddathana 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, thana 'Asim ibn 'Ali, thana Shu'ba, (h) and haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdous ibn Kamil, thana 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, (h) and haddathana Yusuf al-Qadi, thana 'Amr ibn Marzuq, who both said: Thana Shu'ba, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, who said: I heard my father narrating, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Friday prayer on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}; the wording is that of the hadith of 'Asim ibn 'Ali."
"19440","Haddathana Bishr ibn Musa, who said: Thana al-Humaydi, thana Sufyan, thana Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an his father, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}, and he used to recite them both when that coincided with Friday."
"19441","Haddathana Bishr ibn Musa, thana al-Humaydi, thana Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of its meaning, but he did not mention in it: ""'an his father""."
"19442","Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, thana Abu 'Awana, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids and on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}, and sometimes they both fell on one day and he recited them both."
"19443","Haddathana Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, thana Musa ibn Dawud, thana al-Qasim ibn Ma'n, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids and on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}, and sometimes they both fell on one day and he recited them both."
"19444","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Hamza ibn 'Umara al-Asbahani, thana al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim, thana Yahya ibn Ya'la, thana my father, 'an Ghaylan ibn Jami', 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?} on Friday and in the two Eids, and sometimes they both fell on one day and he recited them both together."
"19445","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Jarir, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Eid and on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}, and when two Eids coincided on one day he recited them both together."
"19446","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Waki', 'an Mis'ar and Sufyan, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an his father, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids and on Friday: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}."
"19447","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, thana Ma'mar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi, thana 'Amir ibn Mudrik, thana Isra'il, 'an Jabir, 'an Habib, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in al-Adha and al-Fitr: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?}, and he would often recite them both on Friday."
"19448","Haddathana Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, thana Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, thana Abu 'Awana, 'an Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, meaning al-'Isha: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third night."
"19449","Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man, thana Abu 'Awana, 'an Abi Bishr, 'an Bashir ibn Thabit, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, the 'Isha prayer: al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third night."
"19450","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, anba Hushaym, 'an Abi Bishr, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-'Isha: he used to pray it after the setting of the moon on the third night from the beginning of the month."
"19451","Haddathana Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, thana my father, thana Yazid ibn Harun, anba Shu'ba, 'an Abi Bishr, 'an Bashir ibn Thabit, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I am indeed the most knowledgeable of people about the time of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he used to pray it at about the time the moon disappears on the fourth night. Yazid said: So I said to him: Hushaym narrated it to us as ""on the third night,"" so Yazid said: Put it as a doubt: ""on the third or fourth night."""
"19452","Haddathana 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, thana 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, thana Jarir, 'an Raqaba ibn Masqala, 'an Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyya, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the appointed time of this prayer, the last 'Isha: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third."
"19453","Haddathana Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar, thana Yazid ibn Harun, anba Sa'id ibn Abi 'Aruba, (h) and haddathana Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, thana Dawud ibn Shabib, thana Hammad ibn Salama, 'an Sa'id ibn Abi 'Aruba, 'an Qatada, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl: ""If she had made her lawful to him, then flog him one hundred lashes; and if she had not made her lawful to him, then stone him."""
"19454","Haddathana Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi, thana Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, thana Yazid ibn Harun, 'an Ayyub ibn Abi Miskin and Sa'id ibn Abi 'Aruba, 'an Qatada, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19455","Haddathana Abu Husayn al-Qadi, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, 'an Sa'id ibn Abi 'Aruba, 'an Qatada, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19456","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz al-Basri, thana Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi, (h) and haddathana Yusuf al-Qadi, thana Hudba ibn Khalid, who both said: Thana Hammam, 'an Qatada, 'an Habib ibn Yasaf, 'an Habib ibn Salim, that a man had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and he was brought before al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I shall certainly judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): if she had made her lawful to him, I will flog him one hundred; and if she had not made her lawful to him, I will stone him with stones."
"19457","Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi, thana Habban ibn Hilal, thana Aban ibn Yazid, thana Qatada, haddathani Khalid ibn 'Urfuta, 'an Habib ibn Salim, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that a man called 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, who was nicknamed Farfar or Qarqar, had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, and he was brought before al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I shall certainly judge with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): if she had made her lawful to you, I will flog you one hundred; and if she had not made her lawful to you, I will stone you with stones. And she had made her lawful to him, so he flogged him one hundred."
"19458","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Hushaym, 'an Abi Bishr, 'an Habib ibn Salim, that a man had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl, so she came to al-Nu'man and informed him, and he said: Indeed, I have concerning that a decisive report which I took from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): if you had given him permission, I will flog him one hundred; and if you had not given him permission, I will stone him."
"19459","Haddathana Abu Zur'a 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi, thana Abu Nu'aym, thana Sufyan, (h) and haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, 'an 'Abd al-Razzaq, 'an al-Thawri, 'an Jabir, 'an Abi 'Azib, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Everything is a mistake except the sword, and for every mistake there is compensation."""
"19460","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, thana Nasr ibn 'Ali, thana my father, thana Hazim ibn Ibrahim, 'an Jabir, 'an Abi 'Azib, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no hadd except with the sword."""
"19461","Haddathana Abu Husayn al-Qadi, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana Qays ibn al-Rabi', 'an Jabir, 'an Abi 'Azib, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Everything is a mistake except iron and the sword."""
"19462","Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath, thana my father, 'an Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, 'an Abi Ziyad al-Taymi, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."""
"19463","Haddathana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, 'an al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, 'an Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Jadali, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows, or Allah will surely set your faces against one another on the Day of Resurrection!"" And I saw a man among us joining his shoulder to his brother's shoulder, his knee to his knee, and his foot to his foot."
"19464","Haddathana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana Waki' and al-Muharibi, 'an Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida, haddathani Abu al-Qasim al-Jadali, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his face toward the people and said: ""Straighten your rows, or Allah will surely set your hearts against one another!"""
"19465","Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, thana Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, (h) and haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Abu Hudhayfa, who both said: Thana Sufyan, 'an Mansur, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay' al-Hadrami, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Worship is supplication,"" then he recited: {Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are too proud for My worship will enter Hell, humiliated}. And the wording is that of Abu Hudhayfa."
"19466","Haddathana Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Raqqi, thana Sa'd ibn Hafs al-Kufi, thana Shayban, and haddathana Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, thana Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama, thana 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa, thana Shayban, 'an Mansur, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay' al-Hadrami, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19467","Haddathana Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, thana Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, thana Shu'ba, 'an Mansur, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay' al-Hadrami, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Supplication is worship,"" {And your Lord says: Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are too proud for My worship will enter Hell, humiliated}."
"19468","Haddathana Abu Husayn al-Qadi, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana Jarir, 'an Mansur, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay', 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19469","Haddathana Abu Husayn al-Qadi, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana 'Abdullah ibn Idris, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay', 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Supplication is worship,"" then he recited: {And your Lord says: Call upon Me; I will respond to you}."
"19470","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Abu Mu'awiya and Waki', 'an al-A'mash, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay', 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, supplication is worship,"" then he recited: {And your Lord says: Call upon Me; I will respond to you}."
"19471","Haddathana Abu 'Awana Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi, thana Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Sulayman al-Hadrami al-Misri, thana al-Khasib ibn Nasih, thana Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna, 'an 'Abdullah ibn Dawud, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Dharr, 'an Yusay', 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning His saying: {Indeed, those who are too proud for My worship}, he said: ""For My supplication"" {will enter Hell, humiliated}."
"19472","Haddathana Idris ibn 'Abd al-Karim al-Haddad, thana 'Asim ibn 'Ali, (h) and haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-'Askari Abu 'Ubayda, thana Hawthara ibn Ashras, who both said: Thana 'Uqba ibn 'Abdullah al-Rifa'i, 'an 'Abdullah ibn Burayda, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that his father took him to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! This is al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, and his mother is 'Amra bint Rawaha; I have come to call you to witness a gift I am gifting him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""O Bashir! Do you gift all your children as you gift this one?"" He said: No. He said: ""Do you not love that they should be equal to you in dutifulness?"" He said: Yes, indeed. He said: ""Then call someone other than me to witness."""
"19473","Haddathana Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar and 'Abdullah ibn Najiya, who both said: Thana Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qassas, thana 'Umar ibn 'Ali al-Muqaddami, thana Mis'ar ibn Kidam, who said: I heard my maternal uncle al-Walid ibn 'Uthman narrating, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever inflicts a hadd flogging where there is no hadd is among the transgressors."""
"19474","Haddathana 'Allan ibn 'Abd al-Samad Maghamma, haddathana 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, thana my father, thana Mujammi' al-Ansari, 'an Zakariyya ibn Khalid, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there are doubtful matters between them. So whoever leaves what is doubtful to him of sin will be even more avoidant of what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts of sin will soon fall into what is clear to him. And indeed, sins are Allah's sanctuary; whoever grazes around the sanctuary will soon fall into it."""
"19475","Haddathana Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-'Abbadani, thana Sulayman ibn Harb, and haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Khalid ibn Khidash, who both said: Thana Hammad ibn Zayd, 'an Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal ibn al-Muhallab, 'an his father, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be just among your children,"" saying it three times."
"19476","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana 'Ali ibn al-Madini, thana Mu'adh ibn Hisham, haddathani my father, 'an Qatada, 'an al-Hasan, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day hastening until he reached the mosque, dragging his cloak, while the sun had eclipsed, and he prayed until it cleared, then he said: ""The people of ignorance used to say: The sun and the moon eclipse only for the death of a great one among the great ones of the people of the earth. But the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone; rather, they are two signs among Allah's signs, and a creation among His creation; He brings about in His creation whatever He wills. So whichever of them it is, pray until it clears."""
"19477","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, (h) and haddathana Abu Husayn al-Qadi, thana Yahya al-Himmani, who both said: Thana Abu al-Ahwas, thana 'Asim ibn Sulayman, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Whenever the sun or the moon eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with us until it cleared."
"19478","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Waki', 'an Sufyan, 'an 'Asim, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the eclipse much like this prayer of yours, bowing and prostrating."
"19479","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi, thana 'Amr ibn Hakam, thana Shu'ba, 'an 'Asim, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the eclipse two rak'as."
"19480","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, thana Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri', thana Mu'adh ibn Hisham, haddathani my father, 'an Qatada, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the sun eclipses, pray as the most recent prayer you prayed of the obligatory prayers."""
"19481","Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, thana Muhammad ibn Bakkar, thana 'Anbasa ibn 'Abd al-Wahid, 'an Ayyub ibn 'Utba, 'an Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you sleeps while intending to pray at night, let him place at his right a handful of dust; then when he wakes, let him take some of it with his right hand and cast pebbles to his left."""
"19482","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barra al-San'ani, thana Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus al-San'ani, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Bahir al-Qass mentioning, 'an Wahb ibn Munabbih, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating about al-Raqim: that three men entered a cave, and a piece of the mountain fell upon the mouth of the cave and sealed them in. Then one of them said: O people! Remember whichever of you did a good deed, that Allah in His mercy may have mercy on us. Then one of them said: I did a good deed once: I had workers whom I hired for work of mine, each man among them for a known wage. Then one day a man came to me in the middle of the day, and I hired him for the remainder of the day on the condition of his companions. He worked the rest of his day as one of them worked in his entire day. I deemed it a matter of obligation not to diminish him anything of what I had hired his companions for, because of his exertion in his work. Then one of them said to me: Do you give this one the like of what you gave me, when he worked only half a day? I said: O servant of Allah! I did not undercut you anything of your condition; it is only my wealth, I dispose of it as I will. So he became angry at that, abandoned his wages, and I placed his due in a corner of the house for as long as Allah willed. Then cattle passed by me after that, and I bought with it a young calf of cattle, and I kept it until it grew, then I sold it, then I spent its price on a cow, and it became pregnant, then it bore offspring until it reached what Allah willed. Then after that an old, feeble shaykh whom I did not know passed by me and said to me: I have a due with you. He reminded me until I recognized him, and I said: Yes, it is you I seek; I presented all of it to him and said: This is your due. He said: O servant of Allah! Do not mock me; if you will not give charity to me, then give me my due! I said: By Allah, I am not mocking you; it is indeed your due, I have nothing of it. So I handed it over to him. O Allah, if I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. So the mountain split open until they saw and beheld. Then the other said: I did a good deed once: I had surplus, and hardship struck the people, so a woman came to me seeking kindness from me. I said to her: No, by Allah, nothing short of yourself. She refused me, then she returned and reminded me of Allah, but I refused her. I said: No, by Allah, nothing short of yourself. She refused me. Then she mentioned that to her husband, and he said to her: Give him yourself and enrich your dependents. So she came to me and adjured me by Allah, and I said to her: No, by Allah, nothing short of yourself. When she saw that, she surrendered herself to me. When I uncovered her and was about to take her, she trembled beneath me. I said: What is wrong with you? She said: I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds. So I said to her: You feared Allah in hardship while I did not fear Him in ease?! So I left her and gave her what was due upon me for having uncovered her. O Allah, if I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. So the mountain split open until they recognized and it became clear to them. Then the other said: I did a good deed once: I had two elderly, aged parents, and I had sheep; I would feed my parents and give them drink, then return to my sheep. Then one day rain befell me and detained me, and I did not return until evening. I came to my family, took my milking vessel, milked, and left my sheep standing, and I walked to my parents to give them drink, but I found them asleep. It was hard upon me to wake them, and hard upon me to abandon my sheep. So I did not cease sitting with my milking vessel in my hand until the morning woke them. O Allah, if I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. Al-Nu'man said: It is as if I hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Then the mountain said: Taq! So Allah relieved them and they came out."""
"19483","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barra, who said: Thana Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus, thana Rabah ibn Zayd, 'an 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi 'Asim, 'an Wahb ibn Munabbih, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19484","Haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana 'Ali ibn Bahr, thana Isma'il ibn 'Abd al-Karim, haddathani 'Abd al-Samad ibn Ma'qil, who said: I heard Wahb say: Haddathani al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning al-Raqim; he said: ""Three men were in a cave, and the mountain fell upon the mouth of the cave and sealed it upon them. Then one of them said: Remember whichever of you did a good deed, that Allah may have mercy on him in His mercy. Then a man among them said: I did a good deed once: I had hired laborers working work for me, and I hired each man among them for a known wage. Then one day a man came to me in the middle of the day, and I hired him on the condition of his companions. He worked in the rest of his day as each man among them worked in his entire day. I deemed it a matter of obligation not to diminish him of what I had hired his companions for, because of his exertion in his work. Then a man among them said: You gave this one the like of what you gave me, when he worked only half the day? I said: O servant of Allah! I did not undercut you anything of your condition; it is only my wealth, I dispose of it as I will. So he became angry, went away, and abandoned his wage. I placed his due in a corner of the house for as long as Allah willed. Then cattle passed by me after that, and I bought with it a young she-calf of cattle, and it reached what Allah willed. Then after a while an old, feeble shaykh whom I did not know passed by me and said: I have a due with you. He reminded me until I recognized him, and I said: It is you I seek; this is your due. I presented all of it to him. He said: O servant of Allah! Are you mocking me?! If you will not give charity to me, then give me my due. I said: By Allah, I am not mocking you; it is indeed your due, I have nothing of it. So I handed all of it over to him. O Allah, if I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. So the mountain split open until they saw the light and beheld. Then the other said: I did a good deed once: I had surplus, and hardship struck the people, so a woman came to me seeking kindness from me. I said: By Allah, nothing short of yourself. She refused me and went away, then she returned and reminded me of Allah, but I refused her. I said: No, by Allah, nothing short of yourself. She refused me and rose. Then she mentioned to her husband, and he said to her: Give him yourself and enrich your dependents. So she returned to me and adjured me by Allah, but I refused her. I said: By Allah, nothing short of yourself. When she saw that, she surrendered herself to me. When I uncovered her, she trembled beneath me. I said to her: What is wrong with you? She said: I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds. So I said to her: You feared Him in hardship while I did not fear Him in ease! So I left her and gave her, by the right upon me for having uncovered her. O Allah, if You know that I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. He said: So it split open until they recognized and it became clear to them. Then the other said: I did a good deed once: I had two elderly, aged parents, and I had sheep; I would feed my parents and give them drink, then I returned to my sheep. Then one day rain befell me and detained me, and I did not return until evening. I came, took my milking vessel, milked, with my sheep standing, and I went to my parents and found them asleep. It was hard upon me to wake them, and hard upon me to abandon my sheep. So I did not cease sitting with my milking vessel in my hand until the morning woke them, and I gave them drink. O Allah, if I did that for Your Face, then relieve us. Al-Nu'man said: It is as if I hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: ""The mountain said: Taq, taq! So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, relieved them and they came out."""
"19485","Haddathana Ishaq al-Dabari, 'an 'Abd al-Razzaq, 'an Ibn Jurayj, 'an Ibn Tawus, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Bashir ibn Sa'd, the father of al-Nu'man, with him his son al-Nu'man, and he said: Bear witness that I have gifted him a slave or a slave-girl. He said: ""Do you have a child other than him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then did you gift them the like of what you gifted him?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then I bear witness only to what is right!"""
"19486","Haddathana 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, who said: I read to Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari, thana Rayhan ibn Sa'id, thana 'Abbad ibn Mansur, 'an Ayyub, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an Abi Salih, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: ""Indeed, Allah wrote a Book before He created the heavens and the earth by two thousand years, and it is with the Throne; and He sent down from that Book two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqara. And indeed, Satan does not enter a house in which they are recited for three nights."""
"19487","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, 'an Mu'awiya ibn Salih, who said: Haddathani Nu'aym ibn Ziyad Abu Talha al-Anmari, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir on the minbar of Hims say: We stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the twenty-seventh night until we thought that al-falah would escape us, and we used to consider it the suhur. But you say: the seventh night is the twenty-ninth night, while we say: the seventh night is the twenty-seventh night. So which of us is more correct, we or you?"
"19488","Haddathana Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Qitrani al-Basri, thana Hudba ibn Khalid, thana Hammad ibn Salama, thana Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi, 'an Abi Qilaba, 'an Abi al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah wrote a Book before He created the heavens and the earth by two thousand years, and He sent down from it two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqara. They are not recited in a house for three nights without a devil approaching it."""
"19489","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri, thana Mu'ammal ibn Ihab, thana 'Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi, thana Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Irq al-Yahsibi, 'an his father, 'an al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Grapes from al-Ta'if were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave me a cluster and said: ""Take it to your mother."" But I ate it on the way. Then he said: ""What happened to the cluster?"" I said: I ate it. So he named me Ghudar."
"19490","Haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana 'Ali ibn Bahr, thana Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, 'an Sa'id ibn Sinan, 'an his father, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: Al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to my mother with a cluster of grapes, then he asked me about it afterwards, and I informed him that I had eaten it. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Ghudar."""
"19491","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi, thana Abu Tawba al-Rabi' ibn Nafi', thana Mu'awiya ibn Sallam, 'an Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Aba Sallam say: Haddathani al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: I was at the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except to give drink to the pilgrims. And a man said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except to maintain the Sacred Mosque. And another said: Jihad in the path of Allah is better than what you have said. Then 'Umar rebuked them and said: Do not raise your voices at the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and it was Friday - but when I have prayed Friday I will enter and ask him for a verdict about what you differed over. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Do you make the giving of drink to the pilgrims and the maintenance of the Sacred Mosque like one who believes in Allah} ... the verse."
"19492","Haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Muslim ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Hadrami al-Himsi, thana Muhammad ibn Himyar, thana Safwan ibn 'Amr al-Saksaki, who said: We went out in a funeral procession, and its people were entering it into the grave from the side of the qibla. Then Karib al-Yahsibi said: Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every house has a door, and the door of the grave is from the direction of its feet."""
"19493","Chapter of the letter Waw: Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami al-Qayl; 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father; Musa ibn 'Umayr, from 'Alqama. Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Abu Nu'aym, na Musa ibn 'Umayr al-'Anbari, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an his father Wa'il ibn Hujr, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood in prayer, would grasp his left with his right. He said: And I saw 'Alqama doing it."
"19494","Hujr ibn al-'Anbas, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-'Abbadani, thana Sulayman ibn Harb, na Shu'ba, 'an Salama ibn Kuhayl, 'an Hujr ibn al-'Anbas, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left."
"19495","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Suyuti, thana 'Affan, thana Shu'ba, 'an Salama ibn Kuhayl, 'an Hujr Abi al-'Anbas, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he said: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, he said: Amin, lowering his voice with it."
"19496","Jami' ibn Matar, from 'Alqama. Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, na Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi, (h) and haddathana Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, na Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti, who both said: Anba Jami' ibn Matar, thana 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land in Hadramawt as a fief."
"19497","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Khalifa, who both said: Thana Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi, (h) and haddathana Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, thana Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti, who both said: Na Jami' ibn Matar, who said: Thana 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: We were sitting with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came with a leather strap around his neck, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, this one and my brother were in a well digging it, and the pickaxe fell and struck his companion's head and killed him. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Pardon him."" But he refused. Then he stood and mentioned similar words, and al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Pardon him."" But he refused. Then al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Take him away; if you kill him, you will be like him."" So he went out with him until he passed beyond, then someone called to him: Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says? So he returned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you kill him, you will be like him."" He said: Yes, I pardon him. So he went out dragging his leather strap until he disappeared from us."
"19498","Hamza Abu 'Umar al-'A'idhi, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib, thana Hawdha ibn Khalifa, thana 'Awf ibn Abi Jamila, 'an Hamza Abi 'Umar al-'A'idhi, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man was brought with a leather strap, led along, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the guardian of the slain: ""Do you pardon him?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then will you take the blood-money?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then will you kill him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then take him away."" So he turned away from him. He said: ""Come, will you pardon?"" like his first saying. The guardian of the slain said the like of his saying three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at the fourth: ""Indeed, if you pardon, he will bear your sin and the sin of your companion."" So he left him. He said: And I saw him dragging his leather strap."
"19499","Isma'il ibn Salim, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, thana Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn, (h) and haddathana Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Qitrani, thana al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Rashid al-Wasiti, who both said: Thana Hushaym, 'an Isma'il ibn Salim, who said: And haddathani 'Alqama ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami, 'an his father Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man who had killed a slain man was brought to him, and he handed the killer over to the guardian of the slain to kill him. When he went off with him, with a leather strap around his neck, al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: ""The killer and the slain are in the Fire."" A man went to him and mentioned to him what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, so he let him go free. I saw him when he let him go free, walking off dragging his leather strap. Isma'il said: I mentioned that to Habib ibn Abi Thabit, and he said: From Ibn Ashwa', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that man to pardon, but it is as if he did not do so; then when he was told what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, he let him go."
"19500","'Amr ibn Murra, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father. Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, thana Mu'awiya ibn 'Amr, thana Za'ida, 'an Husayn, who said: Dhakara 'Amr ibn Murra, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, 'an al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning raising his hands for prayer. Husayn said: Then Ibrahim said: I do not know, perhaps Wa'il saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only on that day - so how did he memorize it, while 'Abdullah and his companions did not memorize it? Is he more knowledgeable about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than 'Abdullah? He would only raise his hands at the opening."
"19501","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, thana Khalid, thana Husayn, 'an 'Amr ibn Murra, who said: I entered the mosque of Hadramawt, and there was 'Alqama ibn Wa'il narrating from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands before bowing and after it. I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he became angry and said: He saw him, but Ibn Mas'ud and his companions did not see him?"
"19502","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani, thana al-Yaman ibn Sa'id al-Missisi, thana Ash'ath ibn Shu'ba, thana Warqa' ibn 'Umar, 'an Husayn, who said: 'Amr ibn Murra used to narrate to them, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, raise his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing, do that."
"19503","Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami, thana 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi, haddathani my father, thana Sharik, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he heard al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: {Nor of those who went astray}, say: Amin."
"19504","Simak ibn Harb, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi, who both said: Haddathana 'Amr ibn Marzuq, anba Shu'ba, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land in Hadramawt as a fief."
"19505","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Yahya ibn Ma'in, who said: Thana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, thana Shu'ba, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me land as a fief, and he sent Mu'awiya with me, saying: ""Mark it out for him and give it to him."" Mu'awiya said to me: Let me ride behind you. I said: You are not to be among the riding-companions of kings. He said: Give me your sandal to wear. I said: Wear the shade of the camel. Then when Mu'awiya became caliph, I came to him and he seated me with him on the couch, then he reminded me of the hadith. Simak said: He said: I wished I had carried him in front of me."
"19506","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, (h) and haddathana 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, who both said: Thana 'Asim ibn 'Ali, who both said: Thana Shu'ba ibn al-Hajjaj, that Simak ibn Harb akhbarani, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not call grapes al-karm; rather, say al-habala or al-habl."""
"19507","Haddathana Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi, who both said: Thana 'Amr ibn Marzuq, anba Shu'ba, 'an Simak, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I witnessed al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Suwayd ibn Tariq asked him about wine, and he forbade him. He said: We treat illness with it and it is put into medicine. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not a medicine, but it is a disease."""
"19508","Haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana Sharik, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Yazid ibn Salama came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have many vineyards; may we press them, sell it, and seek cure with it? He said: ""No, it is a disease."""
"19509","Haddathana 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, thana 'Asim ibn 'Ali, (h) and haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, (h) and haddathana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, (h) and haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, who all said: Thana Abu al-Ahwas, thana Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an his father, who said: A man from Hadramawt and a man from Kinda came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has overpowered me regarding land that belonged to my father. The Kindi said: It is my land, in my possession; I cultivate it, and he has no right in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you have proof?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then he has his oath."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is a wicked man who does not care what he swears upon; he does not restrain himself from anything. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have nothing from him but that."" So he went off to swear, and when he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if he swears upon his wealth to consume it unjustly, he will surely meet Allah while He is turned away from him."""
"19510","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana 'Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talha al-Qannad, thana Asbat ibn Nasr, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an his father, that a woman was assaulted by a man in the darkness before dawn while she was heading to the mosque, overpowering her for himself. She sought help from a man who passed by her, and her assailant fled. Then a group of people passed by her and she sought help from them; they caught the one she had sought help from, while the other one outran them. They brought him to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She informed him that he had assaulted her, and the people informed him that they had caught him running hard. He said: I was only helping her against her assailant, but these caught me and seized me. She said: He lies; he is the one who assaulted me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take him away and stone him."" Then a man among the people stood and said: Do not stone him; it is I who did the deed to her. He confessed. So three gathered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the one who had assaulted her, the one who had helped her, and the woman. He said: ""As for you, you are forgiven."" And he said to the one who had helped her a good word. Then 'Umar said: Stone the one who confessed adultery. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, he has repented to Allah with a repentance that, had the people of Yathrib repented it, it would have been accepted from them."""
"19511","Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, thana Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, anba Isra'il, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that a woman went out in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending prayer, and a man met her and satisfied his need from her. She screamed, and he went off. Then a man passed by her, and she said: That man did such-and-such to me. They went and seized the man whom she thought had assaulted her. They said: This one? She said: Yes, it is this one. They brought him to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he ordered him to be stoned, her assailant, the one who had assaulted her, stood and said: I am her man. He said: ""Come near me, for Allah has forgiven you."" And he said to the other man a good word. They said to him concerning the man who had assaulted her: Will you stone him? He said: ""He has repented with a repentance that, had the people of al-Madina repented it, it would have been accepted from them."""
"19512","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Yahya ibn Ma'in, thana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, thana Shu'ba, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Salama ibn Yazid al-Laythi asked, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what if rulers stand over us who ask us for their right and withhold our right from us - what do you command us? He turned away from him, then he asked him and he turned away from him, then he asked him a second or third time, and he said: ""Listen and obey, for upon them is only what they were charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with."""
"19513","Haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Yahya al-Himmani, thana Abu al-Ahwas and Sharik, 'an Simak ibn Harb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Yazid ibn Salama came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering the sermon and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if there are over us people who take us to account for the right but withhold Allah's right from us? Al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent and did not answer him, then he repeated a second time and he did not answer him, then he repeated a third time, and al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Upon him is what he was charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with; if you obey him you will be guided. So listen to him and obey."""
"19514","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, thana Sa'id ibn Sulayman, 'an Yazid ibn 'Ata', 'an Simak, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: A man came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one killed my brother, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""How did you kill him?"" He said: I struck his head with the axe, though I did not intend to kill him. He said: ""Do you have wealth with which to pay his blood-money?"" He said: No. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: ""Take him."" So he went out with him to kill him. Then al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he kills him, he will be like him."" So he returned with him when he heard his saying, and said: Here he is, so command concerning him whatever you will. So al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Release him."""
"19515","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, thana Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, thana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari, thana Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, thana Simak ibn Harb, that 'Alqama ibn Wa'il haddathahu, 'an his father, who said: While I was with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man entered leading another man by a leather strap until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one killed my brother. He said: ""Did you kill him?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""How did you kill him?"" He said: We were gathering firewood from a tree, and he insulted me, so I struck him with the axe on the side of his head and killed him. He said: ""Do you have wealth with which to ransom yourself?"" He said: No; by Allah, I have no wealth except my axe and my cloak. He said: ""Do you think your people will pay on your behalf?"" He said: I am more insignificant to my people than that. So he threw his leather strap to him and said: ""Your companion is yours."" When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he kills him, he will be like him."" Then someone came to him and said: Woe to you! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: ""If he kills him, he will be like him."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I took him only by your command. He said: ""Do you not wish that he should bear his sin and the sin of your companion?"" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Then it is so."" So he threw his leather strap and said: ""Go wherever you wish."""
"19516","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Abu Khalifa, who both said: Thana Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd, thana Ibrahim ibn 'Uthman, thana 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami, 'an his father, who said: Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi and a man from Hadramawt disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land in the possession of al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi, which the Hadrami claimed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Hadrami: ""Your proof."" He said: I have no proof. He said: ""Then if you have no proof, al-Ash'ath will swear."" He said: My right is lost, O Messenger of Allah, if you make it the oath of al-Ash'ath. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath in which he is lying, in order to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man, will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."""
"19517","Haddathana Talib ibn Qurra al-Adhani, thana Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba', (h) and haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Yahya al-Himmani, who both said: Thana Abu 'Awana, 'an 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever seizes a man's land unjustly will meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"19518","'Asim ibn Kulayb, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father. Haddathana Musa ibn Harun, thana al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah, akhbarana Hushaym, 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, he spread his fingers, and when he prostrated, he joined his fingers."
"19519","Qays ibn Sulaym al-'Anbari, from 'Alqama ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti, thana Abu Nu'aym, thana Qays ibn Sulaym al-'Anbari, haddathani 'Alqama ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said takbir when opening the prayer and raised his hands, and when he intended to bow he raised his hands, and after he raised his head from bowing."
"19520","Umm Yahya bint 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, from her uncle 'Alqama. Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami, who said: Haddathatni Maymuna bint Hujr ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I heard my paternal aunt Umm Yahya bint 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, 'an her father 'Abd al-Jabbar, 'an 'Alqama her uncle, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""This is Wa'il ibn Hujr who has come to you; he has not come to you out of desire or fear - he has come out of love for Allah and His Messenger."" And he spread his cloak for him, seated him beside him, drew him to himself, and took him up the minbar and addressed the people, saying to his companions: ""Be gentle with him, for he is newly out of kingship."" I said: My family has overpowered me regarding what is mine. He said: ""I will give it to you, and I will give you double it."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Wa'il ibn Hujr, when you pray, place your hands level with your ears, and a woman places her hands level with her breasts."""
"19521","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami, who said: Haddathatni Maymuna bint Hujr, who said: Haddathatni my paternal aunt Umm Yahya bint 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings to whoever saw me, and whoever saw one who saw me"" - three times."
"19522","'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, from his father; Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il; chapter. Haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, thana 'Abd al-Razzaq, thana Ma'mar, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Nor of those who went astray}, he said: ""Amin,"" until he made us hear it."
"19523","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, thana my father, thana Zuhayr, thana Abu Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I prayed behind him; he began to recite and said: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}. He said: ""Amin,"" aloud."
"19524","Haddathana 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi, thana 'Abdullah ibn Raja', thana Isra'il, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he recited the Opening of the Book and said: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, he said: Amin, raising his voice with it."
"19525","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi, haddathana Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, thana Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he opened with the Opening of the Book, and when he finished it he said: Amin, until those behind him heard."
"19526","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, (h) and haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Yahya al-Himmani, who both said: Thana Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}. He said: ""Amin,"" prolonging his voice with it."
"19527","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, (h) and haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, who both said: Thana Abu al-Ahwas, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he recited the Opening of the Book, and when he finished it he said: ""Amin,"" prolonging his voice with it."
"19528","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, who both said: Thana 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Himsi, who both said: thus; thana Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, who said: Haddathani Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an his father, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I prayed behind him; he began to recite: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}. He said: ""Amin,"" aloud, until I heard him."
"19529","Haddathana Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asbahani, thana Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Harrani, who said: Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salama, 'an Abi 'Abd al-Rahim, 'an Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed behind al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he said: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, he said: ""Amin,"" prolonging his voice with it."
"19530","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, haddathani my father, thana Sa'd ibn al-Salt, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter prayer; when he finished the Opening of the Book he said: ""Amin,"" three times."
"19531","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, who said: Thana Abu Kurayb, thana Sinan ibn Muzahir, thana 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Ja'far al-Farra', 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); whenever he recited: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, he said: ""Amin, that the believing angels may coincide."""
"19532","Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Asbahani, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida, haddathani my father, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he heard al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, say: ""Amin."" Then those behind him said: Amin."
"19533","Haddathana Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud al-Missisi, haddathani my father, thana Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, thana Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an his father, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he recited: {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray}, he said: ""Amin,"" until I heard him while I was behind him."
"19534","Chapter. Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, thana my father, (h) and haddathana Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, thana Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, who both said: Thana Zuhayr, thana Abu Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when making obligatory, raise his hands until they reached his ears."
"19535","Haddathana 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi, thana 'Abdullah ibn Raja', thana Isra'il, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said takbir and raised his hands."
"19536","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, thana Abu al-Ahwas, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he opened the prayer he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears."
"19537","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi, thana Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, thana Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I saw him raise his hands to his ears."
"19538","Haddathana 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, thana 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Himsi, thana Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, 'an Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an his father, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when making obligatory, until they reached below his ears."
"19539","Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Asbahani, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida, thana my father, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands and say takbir."
"19540","Haddathana Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud al-Missisi, haddathani my father, who said: Thana Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, 'an Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an his father, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, raise his hands below his ears."
"19541","Chapter. Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, thana my father, thana Zuhayr, thana Abu Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his right hand in prayer upon his left."
"19542","Haddathana Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, haddathani my father, haddathana Sa'd ibn al-Salt, 'an al-A'mash, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter prayer and say takbir, then place his right forearm upon his left forearm."
"19543","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi, thana Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, thana Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I saw him place the right upon the other."
"19544","Haddathana 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, thana 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Himsi, thana Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, 'an Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his right hand upon his left in prayer, near the wrist."
"19545","Haddathana Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi, thana Luwayn, thana Muhammad ibn Jabir, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaning with one hand upon the other in prayer."
"19546","Haddathana 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi, thana 'Abdullah ibn Raja', anba Isra'il, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard a man say: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed therein. When al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he said: ""Who is the utterer of the words?"" He said: I am, O Messenger of Allah; by Allah, I intended nothing by them but good. He said: ""The gates of heaven were indeed opened for them; nothing held them back short of the Throne."""
"19547","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, (h) and haddathana Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, thana Musaddad, (h) and haddathana al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, thana Yahya al-Himmani, who all said: Thana Abu al-Ahwas, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying when a man came, entered the row, and said: Allah is Most Great, a great takbir, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. When al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam he said: ""Who is the utterer of the words?"" The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah; I intended nothing by them but good. He said: ""I saw the gates of heaven opened; they did not stop short of the Throne."""
"19548","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, (h) and haddathana 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, thana 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who both said: Thana Hubayb ibn Habib, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: Al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer when an entrant entered the prayer and said: Allah is Most Great, a great takbir, and glory be to Allah and with His praise, much. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to heaven, then returned to his prayer until, when he finished the prayer, he said: ""Who is the utterer of the phrase?"" He said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""The gates of heaven were indeed opened for them; nothing held them back short of the Throne."""
"19549","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, thana Abu Kurayb, thana Sinan ibn Muzahir, thana 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Ja'far al-Farra', 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he heard a man say: Allah is Most Great, a great takbir, and glory be to Allah and with His praise, much. When he turned away he said: ""Who is the utterer of the phrase?"" He said: I intended nothing but good. He said: ""The gates of heaven were indeed opened for them; nothing held them back short of the Throne."""
"19550","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Antaki Qarqara, thana Abu al-Mu'afa al-Harrani, thana Muhammad ibn Salama, 'an Abi 'Abd al-Rahim, 'an Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, 'an Abi Ishaq, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: A man stood behind the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and said: Allah is Most Great, a great takbir... then he mentioned the hadith."
"19551","Haddathana Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud al-Missisi, haddathani my father, thana Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, 'an Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, 'an his father, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he heard a man say: Allah is Most Great, a great takbir; praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed therein. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw them, twelve angels vying for them, and the gates of heaven were opened for them."""
"19552","Muhammad ibn Juhada, from 'Abd al-Jabbar. Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (h) and haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz, thana Abu 'Umar al-Hawdi, who both said: Thana Hammam, thana Muhammad ibn Juhada, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he entered prayer he would raise his hands and say takbir, then wrap himself in his garment, then place his right hand upon his left. When he intended to bow, he did thus with his garment, brought out his hands, raised them, said takbir, and bowed. When he intended to prostrate, his knees fell to the ground before his palms. When he prostrated, he placed his forehead between his palms and kept them apart from his sides. Hammam said: And to the best of my knowledge, in the hadith of Muhammad ibn Juhada: ""When he rose, he rose upon his knees and leaned upon his thighs."""
"19553","Haddathana Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn al-Sabbah, thana Abu 'Umar al-Maq'ad, (h) and haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, thana Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab, who both said: Thana 'Abd al-Warith, thana Muhammad ibn Juhada, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, who said: I was a boy who did not comprehend my father's prayer, so haddathani 'Alqama ibn Wa'il, 'an his father Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); whenever he said takbir he would raise his hands, then wrap himself and take his right with his left, entering his hands into his garment. When he intended to raise his head from bowing he would raise his hands. Then he prostrated, placing his forehead between his palms. When he raised his head from prostration he would raise his hands, until he finished his prayer."
"19554","Al-A'mash, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, haddathani my father, thana 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith, thana Hafs ibn Ghiyath, 'an al-A'mash, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating upon the earth, placing his forehead and his nose in his prostration."
"19555","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana al-Muharibi, 'an al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, (h) and haddathana Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, thana al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat, thana 'Imran ibn 'Uyayna, haddathani al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he said takbir in prayer he would raise his hands until he brought them level with his ears."
"19556","Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana Talib ibn Qurra al-Adhani, thana Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba', (h) and haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, haddathani my father, (h) and haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, who all said: Thana Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, thana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: A woman was coerced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he averted the hadd from her and established it upon the one who assaulted her; and it was not mentioned that he assigned her a dower."
"19557","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, thana Muhammad ibn Kharim, 'an al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his nose upon the ground along with his forehead when he prostrated."
"19558","Haddathana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi, thana Sahl ibn 'Uthman, thana 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman, 'an al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that he came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him placing his nose along with his forehead in prostration."
"19559","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, thana Qays ibn al-Rabi', 'an al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, and I saw the trace of his nose along with his forehead in the pebbles."
"19560","Jabir al-Ju'fi, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, thana Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi, thana Abu Tumayla, 'an Abi Hamza, 'an Jabir, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I used to shake hands with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or my skin would touch his skin, and I would smell it on my hands afterwards, for three days, sweeter in scent than musk."
"19561","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, thana Abu Kurayb, thana Mu'awiya ibn Hisham, 'an Shayban, 'an Jabir, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu, sniffed water into his nose and blew it out, and interlaced his fingers with his fingers."
"19562","Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, thana Waki', 'an Mis'ar, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a bucket of water, drank from it, then spat into it."
"19563","Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from 'Abd al-Jabbar. Haddathana Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, thana Abu Kurayb, thana Hani ibn Sa'id al-Nakha'i, 'an Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: I came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and nothing would delight me more than having, in place of my face from him, the face of a man from the desert Arabs. I saw him pray: he would say takbir when he rose and when he prostrated, and he would give salam to his right and to his left when he finished, until I could see the whiteness of his cheek from here and from here."
"19564","Fitr ibn Khalifa, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Abu Nu'aym, thana Fitr, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami, 'an his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, raise his hands until the tips of his thumbs were level with the lobes of his ears."
"19565","Qays ibn al-Rabi', from 'Abd al-Jabbar. Haddathana 'Allan ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-Tayalisi Maghamma, who said: Thana 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi, thana my father, thana Qays, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the burial of hair and nails."
"19566","Al-Mas'udi, from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il. Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, thana al-Mas'udi, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, who said: When my father came to al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he saw him placing his right hand upon his left, and raising his hands with every takbir."
"19567","Haddathana 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, thana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Thana Yazid ibn Harun, thana al-Mas'udi, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate between his palms."
"19568","Haddathana Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, thana 'Amr ibn Marzuq, thana al-Mas'udi, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an some people of his family, 'an his father, that he saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he opened the prayer, place the right upon the left, and hold his palms."
"19569","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, thana Abu Hafs 'Amr ibn 'Ali, thana al-Mas'udi, 'an 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, 'an the people of his house, 'an his father, who said: Whenever al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he would raise his hands along with the takbir."
"19570","Kulayb ibn Shihab Abu 'Asim al-Jarmi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr. Haddathana 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, thana Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, thana Sufyan, 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his right hand upon his left, and when he sat he spread his left foot, placed his forearms upon his thighs, and pointed with the forefinger."
"19571","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, thana Qays ibn al-Rabi', 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I saw al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) open the prayer and say takbir and raise his hands, then take his left with his right. When he intended to bow he said takbir and raised his hands, placing his palms upon his knees and spreading his fingers. When he raised his head he said takbir and raised. When he prostrated he placed his forehead between his palms and set up the toes of his feet. When he rose he folded his left foot and set up the toes of his right foot. When he sat he placed his left palm upon his left thigh and his right elbow upon his right thigh, joined the little finger and the one next to it, made a circle with the middle finger and the thumb, and pointed with the forefinger, supplicating with it."
"19572","Haddathana al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, thana Asad ibn Musa, thana Abu al-Ahwas, thana 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shall certainly memorize the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he opened the prayer he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he took his left with his right. When he said takbir for bowing he raised his hands again as he had raised them for the opening takbir of prayer. When he bowed he placed his palms upon his knees. When he raised his head from bowing he raised his hands again. When he sat for the tashahhud he spread his left foot upon the ground, then sat upon it, placing his left palm upon his left thigh and his right elbow upon his right thigh, then joined his fingers, made a circle with the thumb and the middle finger, then supplicated with the other."
"19573","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, 'an 'Abd al-Razzaq, 'an al-Thawri, 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I observed al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he raised his hands in prayer when he said takbir, then when he said takbir he raised his hands, then when he said: ""Allah hears whoever praises Him,"" he raised his hands. Then he sat and spread his left foot, then placed his left hand upon his left knee and his right forearm upon his right thigh, then pointed with his forefinger, placed the thumb upon the middle finger, circled with it, and clasped his fingers. Then he prostrated, with his hands level with his ears."
"19574","Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, thana Mu'awiya ibn 'Amr, (h) and haddathana Abu Khalifa, thana Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, who both said: Thana Za'ida, 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I said: I shall surely look at how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays. So I looked at him: he said takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then placed his right hand upon the back of his left palm, between the wrist and the forearm. Then when he intended to bow he raised his hands likewise and placed his hands upon his knees. Then he raised his head and raised his hands likewise. Then he prostrated and made his palms level with his ears. Then he sat and spread his left foot, placed his left palm, set the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh, then clasped two of his fingers, made a circle, then raised his finger; and I saw him moving it, supplicating with it. Then I came after that, in a time of cold, and I saw the people, with most garments upon them, moving their hands beneath the garments; the wording is that of the hadith of Mu'awiya ibn 'Amr."
"19575","Haddathana 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, thana Muslim ibn Ibrahim, (h) and haddathana Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, thana Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, who both said: Thana Shu'ba, 'an 'Asim ibn Kulayb, 'an his father, 'an Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami, that he prayed with al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he said takbir he raised his hands; when he prostrated he kept his upper arms away from his sides; and when he sat he spread his left foot and placed his left hand upon his left thigh and his right hand upon his right thigh, and pointed with his glorifying finger; the wording is that of the hadith of Muslim."
"19576","84 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, that his father informed him that Wa'il ibn Hujr informed him: I said: I shall surely observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how he prays. So he stood and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he took hold of his left with his right, then when he intended to bow he raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he placed his palms upon his knees, then he rose and raised his hands likewise, then he prostrated and placed his hands level with his ears, then he prostrated and placed his hands level with his ears, then he sat and spread out his left leg, and placed his left palm upon his left knee, then he placed the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh, and he clenched two (fingers) and made a circle, then I saw him saying thus, and Zuhayr raised his index finger."
"19577","85 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi narrated to us, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer he raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and when he intended to bow and after he raised (his head) from bowing, and when he sat he spread out his left leg and erected the right, and placed his left hand upon his left thigh and his right hand upon his right thigh, and he knotted two (fingers) and made a circle, and gestured thus with the index finger."
"19578","86 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I said: I shall surely observe the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how he prays. So he faced the qiblah and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he took hold of his left with his right, then when he intended to bow he raised them likewise, then he placed his hands upon his knees, then when he raised his head from bowing he raised them likewise, then when he prostrated he placed his head in that position between his hands."
"19579","87 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id al-Asadi, from Asim ibn Kulayb, whose kunyah is Abu Bakr, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I said: I shall surely observe the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how he prays. Then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal."
"19580","88 - al-Hasan ibn Ulail al-Anazi and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he opened the prayer he said the takbir, then he mentioned similar to it."
"19581","89 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both saying: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Musa ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to me, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he said the takbir he raised his hands, and when he intended to bow he raised his hands, and when he intended to prostrate he raised his hands, and when he sat for the tashahhud he would gesture with his index finger."
"19582","90 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il al-Hadrami, he said: I said: I shall surely observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how he prays. So he stood and faced the qiblah and said the takbir and raised his hands until he brought them level with his ears, then he grasped the left with the right, then he bowed and raised his hands and brought them level with his ears, then he placed his palms upon his knees, then he raised his head and raised his hands and brought them level with his ears, then he prostrated and placed his head between his palms, then he prayed another rak'ah like it, then he sat and spread out his left leg, then he supplicated and placed his left palm upon his left knee and his right palm upon his right knee, and he supplicated with the index finger."
"19583","91 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, saying: Shurayh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il al-Qayl, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his right upon his left in prayer."
"19584","92 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he prostrated, he spread out the left (leg) and erected the right."
"19585","93 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated he placed his forehead between his palms."
"19586","94 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Qays, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate, and he erected his feet and kept them aligned."
"19587","95 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he rose (from prostration) he leaned upon one of his hands."
"19588","96 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer he raised his hands level with his ears."
"19589","97 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated he placed his knees before his hands, and he raised his hands before his knees (when rising)."
"19590","98 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ammar ibn Matar narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions in winter; I saw them in burnouses and cloaks, with their hands inside them, raising them to their necks - or he said: to their chests."
"19591","99 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I had (long) hair, so he said: ""Dhubab."" So I went and cut some of my hair, then I came to him, and he said to me: ""Why did you cut some of your hair?"" I said: I heard you say: ""Dhubab,"" and I thought you were finding fault with me. So he said: ""I did not find fault with you; and thus it is better."""
"19592","100 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man in charge of sadaqah, and he came with an emaciated weaned young camel in bad condition, lean, and said: This is from the sadaqah of so-and-so son of so-and-so, of such-and-such (tribe). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""I sent my messenger in charge of sadaqah, and he came to so-and-so; the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the man, so he came with a tall humped she-camel leading it until he came to the son of so-and-so of such-and-such (tribe), who came with this untied young camel. May Allah not bless his camels."" Then it (the she-camel) was conveyed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he led it to him; so he ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""So-and-so son of so-and-so of such-and-such (tribe) was reached by the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came with this tall humped she-camel. May Allah bless him and his camels."""
"19593","101 - Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, from Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Remorse is repentance."""
"19594","102 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Amin aloud."
"19595","Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi from Wa'il ibn Hujr. 103 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I said: I shall surely observe the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would say the takbir when he lowered and when he raised, and he would raise his hands, and salute to his right and to his left."
"19596","104 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr: that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would say the takbir when he lowered and when he raised, and he would raise his hands at the takbir, and salute to his right and to his left. Shu'bah said: Aban ibn Taghlib said to me concerning this hadith: until the brightness of his face appeared; so I mentioned that to Amr ibn Murrah, he said: or similar to that."
"19597","105 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saluting to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek was seen."
"19598","106 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, he said: I prayed behind Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi and he saluted to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left likewise. He said: I said to him: From where did you take this? He said: I prayed behind Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did likewise, until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks."
"19599","107 - al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Utaridi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd Allah al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when He (Allah) said: {Not of those who earned (Your) anger, nor of those who went astray} say: ""My Lord, forgive me. Amin."""
"19600","108 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the killer was brought dragging his strap, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the guardian of the slain: ""Will you pardon him?"" He said: No. He said: ""Will you take (blood-money)?"" He said: No. He said: ""Will you kill him?"" He said: Yes. So he repeated to him three times, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""If you pardon him, he will bear his sin."" He said: So he pardoned him. He said: Then I saw him dragging his strap, having been pardoned."
"19601","Abu al-Anbas from Wa'il ibn Hujr. 109 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu Anbas narrating from Wa'il al-Hadrami, that he prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he said: {nor of those who went astray} he said: ""Amin,"" lowering his voice with it, and he placed his right hand upon his left hand, and saluted to his right and to his left."
"19602","110 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Hujr Abu al-Anbas narrating from Wa'il al-Hadrami, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he said: {nor of those who went astray} he said: ""Amin"" and lowered his voice with it, then he placed his right hand upon the left and placed them upon his belly, and when he said: ""Allah hears whoever praises Him"" he said: ""O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise,"" and he salutes to his right and to his left with two salutations."
"19603","111 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Qabisah narrated to us, (h) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujr ibn al-Anbas al-Hadrami, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: {nor of those who went astray} would say: ""Amin,"" raising his voice with it."
"19604","112 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Anbas, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from his father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I heard him when he said: {nor of those who went astray} say: ""Amin,"" lowering his voice with it, and he placed his right hand upon the left, and he salutes to his right and to his left."
"19605","113 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Sakan Hujr ibn Anbas, he said: I heard Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saluting until I saw the whiteness of his cheek, from this side and from this side."
"19606","114 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Salih, (h) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujr ibn Anbas, from Wa'il, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said Amin aloud, and saluted to his right and to his left until I saw the whiteness of his cheek."
"19607","115 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami, from his father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he saluted to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Thus narrated Musa ibn Qays, from Salamah, saying: from Alqamah ibn Wa'il; and he added in the salam: ""and His blessings."""
"19608","Abu Hariz from Wa'il ibn Hujr. 116 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Hariz, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in pain, until he complained (of illness), pray sitting on his side toward his right."
"19609","Umm Yahya, wife of Wa'il ibn Hujr, from Wa'il ibn Hujr. 117 - Abu Hind Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Hujr ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami narrated to us at Kufah, saying: My uncle Muhammad ibn Hujr narrated to me, saying: My uncle Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to me, from his father Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, from his mother Umm Yahya, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: When the emergence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us, I went forth as a delegate from my people until I came to Madinah. I met his companions before meeting him, and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us glad tidings of you three days before you came to us, saying: ""Wa'il ibn Hujr has come to you."" Then I met him, peace be upon him; he welcomed me, brought my sitting place near, and spread his cloak for me and seated me upon it. Then he called out among the people and they gathered to him, then he ascended the minbar and took me up with him, I being below him. Then he praised Allah and said: ""O people, this is Wa'il ibn Hujr; he has come to you from a distant land, from the land of Hadramawt, obediently, not coerced, a remnant of the sons of kings. May Allah bless you, O Wa'il, and your children and your children's children."" Then he descended and brought me down with him, and lodged me in a dwelling distant from Madinah, and ordered Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan to lodge me in it. I went out and he went out with me until, when we were on part of the road, he said: O Wa'il, the hot ground has burnt the soles of my feet, so mount me behind you. I said: I am not stingy with this she-camel toward you, but you are not of those who ride behind kings, and I dislike being reproached for you. He said: Then throw your sandals to me that I may protect myself with them from the heat of the sun. He said: I am not stingy toward you with these two pieces of leather, but you are not of those who wear the clothing of kings, and I dislike being reproached for you. When I intended to return to my people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered three letters for me: among them a letter exclusively for me preferring me over my people, a letter for me and my household concerning our properties there, and a letter for me and my people. In my exclusive letter: ""In the name of Allah, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to al-Muhajir ibn Abi Umayyah: Wa'il is to be sought out and to move freely among the Aqwal wherever they are of Hadramawt."" And in my letter that is for me and my household: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to al-Muhajir ibn Abi Umayyah: for the sons of Ma'shar and the sons of Dam'aj, the chiefs of Shan u'ah, concerning what they had therein of dominion and pledges, buildings, sea, salt, quarry, whatever property they inherited, spring waters, and whatever property they have therein in Hadramawt, its upper and lower parts, upon protection and neighbourhood; Allah is their protector, and the believers are supporters in that."" And in the letter that is for me and my people: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Wa'il ibn Hujr and the mighty chiefs of Hadramawt: establish prayer and give zakah from the pasturing herd that follows its leader, and its owner has the she-camel given in charity; no driving (of animals to the collector) nor keeping away, no shighar nor wirat in Islam; for every ten of the raiding parties, what the water-skin carries of dates; whoever practises usury has dealt in usury, and every intoxicant is unlawful."" When Mu'awiyah came to rule, he sent a man of Quraysh called Busr ibn Artah, and said to him: I have placed the district under you, so go out with your army; when you have left behind the outskirts of Sham, put your sword (to work): kill whoever refuses my pledge until you reach Madinah, then enter Madinah and kill whoever refuses my pledge, then go out to Hadramawt and kill whoever refuses my pledge; and if you find Wa'il ibn Hujr alive, bring him to me. So he did, and found Wa'il ibn Hujr alive and brought him to him. Mu'awiyah ordered that he be received and gave him permission, and seated him with him upon his couch. Mu'awiyah said to him: Is this couch of mine better or the back of your she-camel? I said: O Commander of the Believers, I was fresh from jahiliyyah and disbelief, and that was the conduct of jahiliyyah; today Allah has brought us Islam, and the conduct of Islam is what you did. He said: What prevented you from aiding us, when Uthman had taken you as a confidant and in-law? I said: You fought a man who had more right to (avenge) Uthman than you. He said: How can he have more right to Uthman than me, when I am closer to Uthman by kinship? I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Ali and Uthman, and a brother has more right than a cousin; and I do not fight the Muhajirun. He said: Are we not Muhajirun? I said: Did we not keep apart from both of you? And another proof: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raised his head toward the east, a large gathering being present with him, then he turned his gaze back to him and said: ""Tribulations will come to you like pieces of the dark night; he made its matter grave and hastened it and deemed it ugly."" I said to him from among the people: O Messenger of Allah, what are the tribulations? He said: ""O Wa'il, when two swords differ in Islam, keep apart from them."" So he said: Have you become a Shi'i? I said: No, but I have become a sincere adviser to the Muslims. Mu'awiyah said: Had I heard that and known it, I would not have brought you here. I said: Did you not see what Muhammad ibn Maslamah did at the killing of Uthman? He gestured with his sword toward a rock and struck it with it until it broke. He said: Those are people who attack us. I said: What shall we do with the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever loves the Ansar, it is by my love, and whoever hates them, it is by my hatred""? So he said: Choose whichever land you wish, for you shall not return to Hadramawt. I said: My kindred are in Sham and my household in Kufah. He said: A man of your household is better than ten of your kindred. I said: I did not stay away from Hadramawt out of delight in it; it is not fitting for the emigrant to return to the place from which he emigrated except for a reason. He said: What is your reason? I said: The saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning tribulations: where you differed, we kept apart from you, and where you unite, we come to you; this is the reason. He said: I have put you in charge of Kufah, so proceed to it. I said: I shall not take charge (of anything) for anyone after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Did you not see that Abu Bakr wanted me and I refused, Umar wanted me and I refused, and Uthman wanted me and I refused, yet I did not abandon their pledge? There came in the letter of Abu Bakr, when the people of our region apostatized, that I stood among them until Allah brought them back to Islam, without (my holding) governorship. So he called Abd al-Rahman ibn Umm al-Hakam and said to him: Go, for I have put you in charge of Kufah, and travel with Wa'il ibn Hujr; honour him and fulfil his needs. He said: O Commander of the Believers, you thought ill of me: you command me to honour a man whom I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) honour, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and you. He said: Then travel with knowledge of that concerning him. So he came with him."
"19610","118 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hujr ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami narrated to us, my uncle Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to me, from his father, from his mother Umm Yahya, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: ""I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a vessel containing water was brought. He poured upon his right (hand) three times, then he immersed his right in the vessel and poured with it upon the left three times, then he immersed the right in the water and scooped a handful of water and rinsed his mouth with it and sniffed water into his nose and blew it out, three times. Then he inserted his palms into the vessel and carried water with them, and washed his face three times, and ran (water) through his beard, and wiped the inside of his ears, then he inserted his little finger inside his ear to convey the water, then he wiped his neck and the inside of his beard with the leftover water of the face. He washed his right forearm three times up to beyond the elbow, and washed the left likewise with the right until beyond the elbow. Then he wiped over his head three times, and wiped the outside of his ears, and wiped his neck and the inside of his beard with the leftover water of the head. Then he washed his right foot three times, and ran (water) between its toes and carried the water beyond the ankle, and raised the water up the leg. Then he did likewise with the left. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and placed it upon his head until it ran down the sides of his head, and said: 'This is the completion of wudu.' Then he entered his prayer-niche and lined the people behind him, and looked to his right and left. Then he raised his hands with the takbir until they touched the lobes of his ears. Then he placed his right upon his left upon his chest. Then he recited al-Hamd aloud until he finished al-Hamd, then he said Amin aloud at his finishing the recitation of al-Hamd until those behind him heard. Then he recited another surah with al-Hamd. Then he raised his hands with the takbir until they touched the lobes of his ears. Then he bent down bowing and placed his palms upon his knees and spread his fingers, and he paused in bowing until his bowing was even and his back became as though a flowing river: had a full cup been placed upon it, it would not have tipped over. Then he raised his head with humility and raised his hands until they touched the lobes of his ears, and said: 'Allah hears whoever praises Him.' Then he stood upright and paused in it until every bone returned to its place. Then he bent down with the takbir prostrating, and fixed his forehead upon the ground and his nose until he saw the trace of his nose in the dust, and he spread his forearms with his head between them. Then he raised his head with the takbir and sat a light sitting, and tucked his left thigh under and erected his right foot, fixing its toes. Then he bent down prostrating likewise. Then he raised his head with the takbir. Then he did likewise in the whole prayer until four rak'ahs were completed. Then he sat in the tashahhud and placed his right palm upon his right knee and lowered his thigh and made a circle with his finger, supplicating with it from beneath the garment; and that was in winter, and his companions were behind him with their hands in their garments doing this. And he performed supererogatory (prayer), then saluted to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen, then saluted to his left until the whiteness of his left cheek was seen."""
"19611","119 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, he said: My family narrated to me, from my father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of water; he drank, then he spat (water from his mouth) into the bucket, then he poured (it) into the well - or: he drank from the bucket, then he spat into the well - and there emanated from it (a fragrance) like the scent of musk."
"19612","120 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, from some of his family, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought a bucket; he performed wudu from it, rinsed his mouth, then spat musk into it - or: sweeter than musk - and blew his nose outside it."
"19613","Those named Wathilah: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' al-Laythi, his kunyah Abu al-Asqa'; and it is said: Abu Qirsafah, and it is said: Abu Shaddad. He used to reside in Sham, at Damascus; he is Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Yalil ibn Nashib ibn Ghayrah ibn Sa'd ibn Layth ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah. 121 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, he said: Maslamah ibn Abd al-Malik addressed us and said: Do not fast Ramadan while travelling; whoever fasts, let him make it up. Abu al-Fayd said: So I met Abu Qirsafah Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and asked him, and he said: Had I fasted, then fasted, then fasted, I would not make it up."
"19614","122 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Marwan ibn Janah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us, saying: I met Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and greeted him, and said: How are you, O Abu Shaddad, may Allah keep you well? He said: Well, O son of my brother."
"19615","123 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Habib ibn Umar al-Ansari narrated to me, my father informed me, saying: I met Wathilah on the day of Eid and said: May Allah accept from us and from you. He said: Yes; may Allah accept from us and from you."
"19616","124 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Habib ibn Umar al-Ansari narrated to me, my father narrated to me, saying: I asked Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' about prayer behind a Qadari. He said: Do not pray behind him; as for me, had I prayed behind him I would have repeated my prayer."
"19617","125 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: ""Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' died in the year eighty-five, his age ninety-eight years."""
"19618","126 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khalid narrated to me, saying: ""Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' died in the year eighty-three, being one hundred and five years old."""
"19619","What Wathilah narrated: Makhul al-Shami from Wathilah. 127 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Umayyah al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not express gloating over your brother, lest Allah cure him and try you."""
"19620","128 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, he said: I entered, I and Abu al-Azhar, upon Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', and we said to him: O Abu al-Asqa', narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no error, no addition, and no forgetfulness. He said: Did any of you recite anything of the Quran tonight? We said: Yes, yet we do not memorise it perfectly; we add the waw and the alif and omit. He said: This Quran is written before you; you do not stint in memorising it, yet you claim that you add and omit. So what of hadiths we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), perhaps we heard them from him only once? It suffices you, when we narrate the hadith to you, (that it be) upon the meaning."
"19621","129 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Yahya ibn al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells a defect without naming it remains in the anger of Allah, and the angels continue to curse him."""
"19622","130 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, (h) and Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, both from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People will be mustered as troops: a troop in Yemen, a troop in Sham, a troop in the east, and a troop in the west."" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a young youth; perhaps I shall live to see that, so which of them do you command me? He said: ""Hold to Sham, for it is Allah's choicest of His lands; He drives to it His choicest of His servants. Hold to Sham, for Allah has guaranteed Sham and its people for me; whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen."""
"19623","131 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every building is a calamity upon its owner except what was like this"" - and he gestured with his palm - ""and every knowledge is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection except one who acted upon it."""
"19624","132 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Anazi narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out to us, and we were merchants, and he would say: ""O company of merchants, beware of lying."""
"19625","133 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Line up, and let the best of you lead you in prayer, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chooses from the angels and from mankind."""
"19626","134 - al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuma ni narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man should not wipe his forehead until he finishes his prayer, and there is no harm in wiping sweat from his temples, for the angels invoke blessings upon him so long as the trace of prostration is between his eyes."""
"19627","135 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever slanders a dhimmi will be flogged for him on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire."" So I said to Makhul: What is the gravest that is said? He said: It is said to him: ""O son of the disbeliever."""
"19628","136 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari, and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, saying: Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Shami, from Makhul, from Wathilah, meaning Ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Keep your children, your insane, your buying and selling, your disputes, the raising of your voices, the carrying out of your hadd punishments, and the unsheathing of your swords away from the mosques; perfume them (with incense) on Fridays, and place places of purification at their doors."""
"19629","137 - al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, while they were consulting him about (a place of) residence, and he gestured toward Sham. Then they asked him, and he gestured toward Sham. Then they asked him, and he gestured toward Sham. He said: ""Hold to Sham, for it is the choicest of Allah's lands; His best of His creation dwell in it. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from his ponds, for Allah has guaranteed Sham and its people for me."""
"19630","138 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Shami informed us, from al-Ala ibn Kathir, from Makhul, he said: We entered upon Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""I heard Mu'adh and Hudhayfah consulting the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about (a place of) residence, and he gestured to them toward Sham. Then they consulted him, and he gestured to them toward Sham. Then they consulted him, and he gestured to them toward Sham. He said the third time: 'Hold to Sham, for it is the choicest of Allah's lands; His best of His servants dwell in it. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from his ponds, for Allah has guaranteed Sham and its people for me.'"""
"19631","139 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, from Bakkar ibn Tamim, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is bright, neither hot nor cold; there is no cloud in it, no rain, no wind, no star is pelted in it; and among the signs of its day, the sun rises without rays."""
"19632","140 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah will raise on the Day of Resurrection a servant who has no sin, and Allah will say: Which of the two matters is dearer to you, that I reward you for your deed or for My favour upon you? He will say: My Lord, You know that I did not disobey You. He will say: Take My servant by one of My favours, and no good deed of his will remain but that favour will consume it. Then he will say: My Lord, by Your favour and Your mercy. He will say: By My favour and My mercy. And a servant will be brought who deems himself righteous and sees no sin for himself, and He will say to him: Did you befriend My friends? He will say: I was at peace with people. He will say: Did you show enmity to My enemies? He will say: My Lord, there was nothing between me and anyone. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: My mercy is not attained by one who does not befriend My friends and show enmity to My enemies."""
"19633","141 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield, and it is a fortress among the fortresses of the believer; every deed is for its doer except fasting. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it."""
"19634","142 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The worst of gatherings are the markets and the roads, and the best of gatherings are the mosques; if you do not sit in the mosque, keep to your house."""
"19635","143 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuma ni narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Makhul narrated to us, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the worst of gatherings are the markets and the roads, and the best of gatherings are the mosques; if you do not sit in the mosque, keep to your house."""
"19636","144 - al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: A questioner asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is the matter with Friday, that the call to prayer is made in it at midday though you forbade (prayer) on other days? He said: ""Allah stokes Hell every day at midday, and quenches it on Friday."""
"19637","145 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not withhold from Allah's servants surplus water, pasture, nor fire, for Allah made them common for the travellers in the wilderness, and a strength for the weak."""
"19638","146 - al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, Bishr ibn Awn narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah sends angels on Friday at the doors of the mosques; they record the people, the first, the second, the third, the fourth, the fifth, and the sixth. When they reach the seventh, they are in the rank of one who offers sparrows (a paltry offering)."""
"19639","147 - And with his chain, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to seek understanding in religion."
"19640","148 - And with his chain, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us not to sit in circles on Friday before the emergence of the imam, but let them face the qiblah; nor on the day of the two Eids after the prayer."
"19641","149 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Taqi narrated to us, both saying: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Umar al-Dimashqi, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, a feast was prepared for him; he ate reclining and applied depilatory paste (or: smeared himself), then the sun struck him, so he put on the sunshade."
"19642","150 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let none of you say: I spilled water; rather let him say: I urinate."""
"19643","151 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Shababah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bakr al-Shaybani narrated to us, Bistam ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Uruzzi narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: When the dead person was placed in his grave, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: ""In the name of Allah, and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)""; and he placed a clod behind the back of his neck, a clod between his shoulders, (one) between his knees, and another behind him."
"19644","152 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hold to pumpkin, for it increases the brain; and hold to lentils, for they were blessed upon the tongues of seventy prophets."""
"19645","153 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Mutual gratification between women is adultery between them."""
"19646","154 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hakim ibn Khidham narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Kathir, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: There came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man, bald-fronted, cross-eyed, hunch-necked, knock-kneed, protruding-chested, left-handed, bow-legged, splay-footed, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what Allah has made obligatory upon me. When he informed him, he said: I covenant with Allah not to add to His ordinance. He said: ""Why?"" He said: Because He created me bald-fronted, cross-eyed, protruding-chested, left-handed, bow-legged, splay-footed. Then he turned away, and Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Muhammad, where is the one who reproaches his Lord? He reproached a Generous Lord, and He accepted his excuse. He said: Say to him: Will you not be pleased to be raised in the form of Jibril on the Day of Resurrection? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for the man and said: ""You reproached a Generous Lord, and He accepted your excuse. Will you not be pleased that Allah raises you on the Day of Resurrection in the form of Jibril?"" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then I covenant with Allah that my body shall not be able to bear anything that pleases Allah but I shall bear it."
"19647","155 - al-Hajjaj ibn Imran narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Wathilah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, would say: ""Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You."""
"19648","156 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hakim ibn Khidham narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Kathir, from Makhul, from Wathilah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever does not run water between his fingers, Allah will run (them) with fire on the Day of Resurrection."""
"19649","157 - al-Husayn ibn Sumayda' narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Wathilah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever sells a defect without making it clear remains in the hatred of Allah"" - or he said: ""The angels continue to curse him."""
"19650","158 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, he said: I entered, I and Abu al-Azhar, upon Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', and we said: O Abu al-Asqa', narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in which there is no error, no addition, and no forgetfulness. He said: Did any of you recite anything of the Quran tonight? We said: Yes, yet we do not memorise it perfectly; we add the waw and the alif and omit. He said: This Quran is written before you; you do not stint in memorising it, yet you claim that you add and omit. So what of hadiths we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), perhaps we heard them from him only once? It suffices you, when we narrate the hadith to you, (that it be) upon the meaning."
"19651","Shaddad Abu Ammar from Wathilah. 159 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ammar, he said: I was sitting with Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' when they mentioned Ali and reviled him. When they stood up, he said: Sit until I inform you about this one whom they reviled. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day when Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn came; he cast over them a cloak of his, then said: ""O Allah, these are my household; O Allah, remove defilement from them and purify them thoroughly."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, and I? He said: ""And you."" He said: By Allah, it is the most firmly trusted of my deeds in my view."
"19652","160 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Tinnisi narrated to us, both saying: al-Awza'i narrated to us, Abu Ammar Shaddad narrated to us, saying: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' al-Laythi said: I wanted Ali but did not find him; Fatimah said: He went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), calling him to come. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and they entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hasan and Husayn, and seated each of them upon his thigh, and brought Fatimah near his lap. Then he wrapped his garment over them, I being leaning back. Then he said: {Allah only intends to remove defilement from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}. Then he said: ""These are my family; these are my family, most deserving."" Wathilah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I of your family? He said: ""And you are of my family."" Wathilah said: It is among the most hopeful of what I hope for."
"19653","161 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Tinnisi narrated to us, all saying: al-Awza'i narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Ammar narrated to us, saying: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah chose Banu Kinanah from Banu Ismail, chose Quraysh from Kinanah, chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."""
"19654","162 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Ammar narrated to us, that Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' narrated to him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me. He turned away from him twice. The prayer was established; when he saluted, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Did you not perform wudu when you came?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""And did you pray with us?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then go, for Allah has pardoned you."""
"19655","163 - Abu Ammar Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Shaddad Abi Ammar, from Abi Umamah, similar to it."
"19656","Rabi'ah ibn Yazid from Wathilah. 164 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, that he heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Among the greatest fabrications are three: that one fabricate concerning one's eyes, saying: I saw, though he did not see; that one fabricate by being ascribed to other than one's father; or that one say: By my hearing, though he did not hear."""
"19657","165 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, both saying: Rabi'ah ibn Yazid al-Rahabi narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it, Allah writes for him two shares of reward; and whoever seeks knowledge and does not attain it, Allah writes one share of reward."""
"19658","166 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, that Rabi'ah ibn Yazid narrated to him that he heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""You claim that I am the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to depart; then you will come after me in scattered groups, some of you killing others."""
"19659","167 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: ""You claim that I am of the last of you to die, but I am of the first of you to die; you will follow me in scattered groups, some of you striking the necks of others."""
"19660","168 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim and Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, (h) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hiq l ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, saying: Rabi'ah ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: ""You claim that I am of the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die; and you will follow me in scattered groups, some of you destroying others."""
"19661","Abu Bakr ibn Bashir from Wathilah. 169 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Isa ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Bashir, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever comes to a soothsayer and asks him about something, repentance is veiled from him for forty nights; if he believes him in what he says, he has disbelieved."""
"19662","Busr ibn Ubayd Allah from Wathilah. 170 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, (h) and Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, (h) and Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati and Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, both saying: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I was among the people of al-Suffah; I saw us with none of us having a complete garment, and sweat had taken hold in our skins along with dust and dirt, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: ""Let the poor of the Muhajirun receive glad tidings."" Then a man came wearing fine attire, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not speak a word but his soul burdened him to come with speech surpassing the speech of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he departed, he said: ""Allah does not love this one and his voice; they twist their tongues for people as the cow twists its tongue in the pasture; likewise Allah will twist their tongues and faces in the Fire."""
"19663","Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri from Wathilah. 171 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Habib ibn Adrak, that Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhibb informed him that Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri informed them, saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Among the gravest fabrications is that one ascribes to me what I did not say, that one shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see, and that one claims (descent) to other than one's father."""
"19664","172 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, (h) and Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both saying: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht al-Makki, from Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the gravest fabrications is that one ascribes to me what I did not say, that one claims (descent) to other than one's father, and that one shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see."""
"19665","173 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father, saying: Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri narrated to me, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The greatest fabrication before Allah is that one says concerning me what I did not say, claims (descent) to other than one's patrons, or shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see."""
"19666","174 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, saying: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, saying: I heard Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The gravest fabrication is that one fabricates concerning me what I did not say, that one shows one's eyes what they did not see, and that one claims (descent) to other than one's father."""
"19667","175 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19668","176 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Habib ibn Adrak, from Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, from Wathilah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19669","177 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, from Wathilah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19670","178 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, (h) and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman informed us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the greatest fabrications is that one claims (descent) to other than one's father, or shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see, or says concerning Allah and His Messenger what they did not say."""
"19671","179 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h) and Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, saying: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, that he heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The greatest fabrication is that it be fabricated concerning me what I did not say, or a man claims (descent) to other than his father, or shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see."""
"19672","180 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the greatest fabrications is that a man says concerning me what I did not say, or claims (descent) to other than his father, or shows one's eyes in a dream what they did not see."""
"19673","181 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb informed us, Umar ibn Ru'bah informed us, saying: I entered with Abu Salamah al-Himsi upon him, and he narrated to me from Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""A woman takes three inheritances: her freed slave, her foundling, and the child against whom there is no imputation."""
"19674","182 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Himsi Sulayman ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Umar ibn Ru'bah, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19675","183 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, (h) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Idris ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, both saying: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, all saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Yazid ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abd al-Wahhab al-Makki, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The Muslim is inviolable to the Muslim: his blood, his honour, and his property. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor abandon him. Taqwa is here"" - and he pointed with his hand to the heart - ""and it suffices a man as evil to despise his Muslim brother."""
"19676","184 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, (h) and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ru'bah, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever establishes a good practice, his is its reward for as long as it is acted upon in his life and after his death until it is abandoned; and whoever establishes an evil practice, upon him is its sin until it is abandoned. Whoever dies as a guard on the frontier in the path of Allah, the reward of the frontier-guard continues for him until he is raised on the Day of Resurrection."""
"19677","Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali from Wathilah. 185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The scrolls of Ibrahim were sent down on the first night of the month of Ramadan, the Torah was sent down six (nights) past of Ramadan, the Gospel was sent down thirteen past of Ramadan, the Psalms were sent down eighteen elapsed of Ramadan, and the Quran was sent down twenty-four elapsed of Ramadan."""
"19678","186 - Yusuf al-Qadi and al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was given the Seven in place of the Torah, I was given the Mathani in place of the Psalms, and I was favoured with the Mufassal."""
"19679","187 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was given the Seven Long ones in place of the Torah, I was given the Mathani in place of the Gospel, I was given the Mi'in in place of the Psalms, and I was favoured with the Mufassal."""
"19680","188 - al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There shall enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my ummah more than Banu Tamim."""
"19681","189 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri narrated to us, (h) and Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, all saying: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, saying: Layth informed us, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was commanded with the siwak until I feared it would be prescribed upon me."""
"19682","190 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim and Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was commanded with the siwak until I feared it would be prescribed upon me."""
"19683","191 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, (h) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd from the hudud of Allah, so establish Allah's hadd in me. He turned away from him, then he came to him a second time and he turned away from him, then he came to him a third time and he turned away from him; then the prayer was established. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd from the hudud of Allah, so establish Allah's hadd in me. He said: ""Did you not perform wudu and perfect the wudu, purify yourself and perfect the purification, and witness the prayer with us just now?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Go, for it is your expiation."""
"19684","192 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bedouin entered and said: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and have mercy on no one with us. They said to him: Woe to you, woe to you; you have restricted what is spacious. Then the bedouin withdrew and urinated standing, and they rushed toward him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave him until he finishes his urination."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a bucket of water and poured it upon his urine."
"19685","193 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Ubayd ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I showed myself to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Mosque of al-Khayf, and his companions said to me: Away from you, O Wathilah - meaning: move away from the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave him, for he has come only to ask."" So I drew near and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, give us a fatwa about a matter we shall take from you after you. He said: ""Let your own soul aid you."" He said: How can I do that? He said: ""Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, even if the muftis give you fatwa."" I said: How can I know that? He said: ""Place your hand upon your heart, for the heart is at rest with the lawful and is not at rest with the unlawful; and the Godfearing Muslim leaves the small out of fear of falling into the grave. "" I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, what is partisanship? He said: ""One who aids his people in wrongdoing."" I said: Who is the greedy? He said: ""One who seeks earning without lawful means."" I said: Who is the Godfearing? He said: ""One who stops at the doubtful."" I said: Who is the believer? He said: ""One whom people trust with their properties and blood."" I said: Who is the Muslim? He said: ""One from whose tongue and hand people are safe."" I said: Which jihad is best? He said: ""A word of wisdom before an unjust ruler."""
"19686","Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah from Wathilah. 194 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Awn ibn Abd Allah, he said: I met Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and said: Nothing brought me to Sham but you, so narrate to me from what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O Allah, have mercy on us and forgive us""; and he forbade us to pray facing graves or to sit upon them."
"19687","Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Wathilah. 195 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani narrated to me, saying: Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to me, saying: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: a swallowing in the east, a swallowing in the west, a swallowing in the Arabian Peninsula, the Dajjal, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, Ya'juj and Ma'juj, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, and a fire emerging from the depths of Aden driving the people to the gathering, gathering the tiny creatures and the ants."""
"19688","196 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I went out emigrating to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the people came, some going out and some standing, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see no seated person but he drew near to him and asked: Do you have any need? He began with the first row, then the second, then the third, until he drew near to me and said: ""Do you have any need?"" I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""What is your need?"" I said: Islam. He said: ""It is better for you."" He said: ""And will you emigrate?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""The emigration of the desert or the decisive emigration?"" I said: Which of them is better? He said: ""The decisive emigration is that you remain with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the emigration of the desert is that you return to your desert, with hearing and obedience upon you in your hardship and ease, in what you dislike and what you like, and in preference over you."" He said: So I extended my hand to him and pledged allegiance to him. He said: And he made an exception for me when I had not made an exception for myself, saying: ""In what you are able."" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out for the expedition of Tabuk, and I went out to my family and found my father sitting in the sun with his back to it. I greeted him with the greeting of Islam, and he said: Have you left (the religion)? I said: I have become Muslim. He said: Perhaps Allah will bring good for you and us in it; I was content with that from him. While I was with him, my sister came greeting me, and I said: O my sister, provision me with a woman's provisioning of her brother going to battle. She brought me dough in a bucket, the bucket in a provision-bag. I came forward, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having already departed, and I kept calling: Is there none to carry a man for his share? An old man of the Ansar called to me and said: His share is ours, provided we carry him in turns, with his food with us. I said: Yes; travel with the blessing of Allah. I went out with the best of companions for me: he increased me in carrying beyond what I had stipulated, and favoured me with food apart from what I ate with him, until Allah gave us spoils and I received young she-camels. I drove them until I came to him, he being in his tent. I called him, and he came out and sat upon a pack of his camels' packs. Then he said: Drive them away (from me). So I drove them away. Then he said: Drive them toward me. So I drove them toward me. He said: I see your young she-camels only as noble. He said: I said: They are but your spoils which I stipulated for you. He said: ""Take your young she-camels, O son of my brother, for we intended other than your share."""
"19689","Tawus al-Yamani from Wathilah. 197 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Kindi narrated to me, from Tawus, from Wathilah, he said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, inform me. He said: ""If you wish, I shall inform you of what you came to ask about, and if you wish, then ask."" He said: I said: Rather inform me, O Messenger of Allah, for it is more pleasing to myself. He said: ""You came to ask about certainty and doubt."" He said: I said: That is it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Certainty is what settles in the chest and the heart is at rest with it, even if the muftis give you fatwa. Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for good is tranquillity and doubt is unease; when you doubt, leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what is partisanship? He said: ""That you aid your people in wrongdoing; the Godfearing is one who stops at doubtful matters; the greedy for this world is one who seeks it without lawful means; and sin is what rankles in the chest."""
"19690","Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Adam from Wathilah. 198 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdun ibn Khalid al-Qarqasani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Adam al-Dimashqi narrated to us, from Abu al-Darda, Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', Abu Umamah, and Anas ibn Malik, they said: We were in a gathering of some Jews, discussing qadar, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us angry; he frowned, rebuked, and scowled, then said: ""Quiet! Fear Allah, O ummah of Muhammad: two deep-bottomed dark valleys; the blaze of the Fire will not subside for you."" Then he ordered the Jews to stand, then he stood and spread his right and extended his left finger, then said: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: this is a book from Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, with the names of the people of Paradise, the names of their fathers, mothers, and tribes. Your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished. I have offered excuse, I have warned. O Allah, I have conveyed."""
"19691","Ma'ruf Abu al-Khattab from Wathilah. 199 - Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Mutayyib al-Missisi narrated to us, saying: Sulaym ibn Mansur ibn Ammar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ma'ruf Abi al-Khattab, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: When I became Muslim, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: ""Go and wash with water and lote, and cast off from yourself the hair of disbelief."""
"19692","200 - Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Mutayyib narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Mansur narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ma'ruf, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to the woman under him (his wife): ""Upon you is calmness and dignity."""
"19693","Junah Abu Marwan, freedman of al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik, from Wathilah. 201 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The child belongs to the (marriage) bed, and the stone is for the adulterer; and a woman may not dispose of anything of her property except with her husband's permission."""
"19694","202 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, (h) and Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The best of your youth is one who resembles your elders, and the worst of your elders is one who resembles your youth."""
"19695","203 - Ubayd al-Ijl and Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, both saying: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, forgive the mu'adhdhins and guide the imams."""
"19696","204 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim put in charge of any affair of the Muslims but Allah sends to him two angels directing him aright so long as he upholds the truth; when he intends injustice deliberately, they leave him to himself."""
"19697","205 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, both from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine among women, and said: ""Expel them from your houses."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled al-Habashah, and Umar expelled so-and-so."
"19698","206 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Hammad, freedman of Banu Umayyah, from Junah, freedman of al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: I heard that Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman may not dispose of anything of her property except with her husband's permission when he owns her bond (of marriage)."""
"19699","207 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim Abu Abd al-Malik al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, (h) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, (h) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, both saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amir narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will remain in good so long as among you are those who saw one who saw me and accompanied me."""
"19700","Sulayman ibn Hayyan al-Adawi from Wathilah. 208 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Hayyan al-Adawi narrated to us, saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: I was of the people of al-Suffah; my companions complained of hunger and said: O Wathilah, go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seek food for us. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my companions complain of hunger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O A'ishah, have you anything?"" She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only crumbs of bread. He said: ""Bring it."" She came with a bag; the Messenger of Allah called for a platter, poured the bread into the platter, then began preparing tharid with his hands, it increasing until the platter was full. He said: ""O Wathilah, go and bring ten of your companions, you being the tenth of them."" So I went and brought ten of my companions, I being the tenth of them. He said: ""Sit; take in the name of Allah; take from around it, and do not take from its top, for blessing descends from its top."" They ate until they were full, then they stood, with in the platter the like of what was in it. Then he began preparing it with his hand, it increasing until it was full. He said: ""O Wathilah, go and bring ten of your companions."" So I brought ten. He said: ""Sit."" They sat and ate until they were full, then they stood. He said: ""Go and bring ten of your companions."" So I went and brought ten, and they did likewise. He said: ""Has anyone remained?"" I said: Yes, ten. He said: ""Go and bring them."" So I went and brought them; he said: ""Sit."" They sat and ate until they were full, then they stood, with remaining in the platter the like of what was in it. Then he said: ""O Wathilah, take this to A'ishah."""
"19701","Hayyan Abu al-Nadr from Wathilah. 209 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ubaydah, from Hayyan Abi al-Nadr, he said: I met Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am with My servant's thought of Me; if he thinks good, (good); and if he thinks evil, (evil)."""
"19702","210 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, (h) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, saying: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Hayyan Abi al-Nadr, he said: I heard Wathilah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am with My servant's thought of Me, so let him think of Me what he wills."""
"19703","211 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Sa'ib, he said: I heard Hayyan Aba al-Nadr narrating from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am with My servant's thought of Me; let My servant think what he wills."""
"19704","Abu Sa'd al-Dimashqi from Wathilah. 212 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah informed us, Abu Sa'd narrated to us, saying: I saw Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' enter the mosque of Damascus and pray in it, and spit beneath his left foot, then rub it. When he departed, I said to him: Do you spit in the mosque while you are of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: ""Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."""
"19705","Bishr ibn Hayyan from Wathilah. 213 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, (h) and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, (h) and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, all saying: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Hayyan, he said: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' came to us while we were building a mosque; he stood over us and greeted, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever builds for Allah a mosque in which prayer is performed, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise better than it."""
"19706","Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas from Wathilah. 214 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, (h) and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, (h) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, all saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Marwan ibn Janah narrated to us, saying: I heard Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his prayer over a man of the Muslims: ""O Allah, so-and-so is in Your protection and the rope of Your neighbourhood; so protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. You are the people of faithfulness and truth. O Allah, forgive him and have mercy on him; You are the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful."""
"19707","215 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, he said: We entered upon Yazid ibn al-Aswad visiting him; Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' entered upon him, and when he looked at him he extended his hand and wiped with it his face and chest, having pledged allegiance with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Wathilah said: ""How is your thought of your Lord?"" He said: Good. He said: Then receive glad tidings, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah says: ""I am with My servant's thought: if good, then good; and if evil, then evil."""
"19708","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qasimah from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa'. 216 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla and Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar informed us, saying: Umar ibn al-Darafs narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qasimah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', that he narrated to him, saying: I was in al-Suffah, they being twenty men; hunger struck us, I being the youngest of the people in age. They sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to complain to him of their hunger. He looked in his house and said: ""Is there anything?"" They said: Yes, here is a morsel and some milk. He said: ""Bring it to me."" He crumbled the morsel into fine crumbs, then poured the milk upon it, then carried it with his hand until he made it like tharid. Then he said: ""O Wathilah, call ten of your companions for me, leaving ten."" So I did. Then he said: ""Sit, in the name of Allah."" They sat; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the top of the tharid and said: ""Eat from around it, in the name of Allah; blessing comes to it from above it, for it is extended."" He said: I saw them eating, licking their fingers, until they were fully sated. When they finished, he said to them: ""Go to your place and send your companions to me."" I stood marvelling at what I saw. He turned to the ten and ordered them likewise; they ate until they were fully sated, with in it a surplus."
"19709","Abu Siba' from Wathilah. 217 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, both saying: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Malik, he said: Abu Siba' informed us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""It is not lawful for anyone to sell a thing without making clear what is in it."""
"19710","al-Gharif ibn al-Daylami from Wathilah. 218 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Gharif, meaning a man of the family of Ibn al-Daylami, he said: We came to Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith in which there is no addition nor omission. He became angry and said: ""One of you recites with his copy hung in his house, adding and omitting."" We said: We intended only that you narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no one between you and him. He said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a companion of ours who had become deserving (of the Fire). He said: ""Free (a slave) on his behalf; Allah will free with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."""
"19711","219 - And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Gharif ibn al-Daylami, he said: We came to Wathilah ibn al-Asqa'; he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it, without mentioning al-Awza'i."
"19712","220 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, al-Gharif ibn Ayyash ibn Fayruz al-Daylami narrated to me, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk; people of Banu Sulaym came and said: O Messenger of Allah, a companion of ours has become deserving (of the Fire). He said: ""Let a neck be freed on his behalf; Allah will ransom with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."""
"19713","221 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, al-Gharif ibn Ayyash ibn Fayruz al-Daylami narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa': that a group of Banu Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A companion of ours has become deserving (of the Fire). He said: ""Let a neck be freed on his behalf; Allah will ransom with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."""
"19714","222 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hibban narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Fayruz al-Daylami, from al-Gharif ibn Ayyash, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning a man who has become deserving - meaning the Fire? He said: ""He frees a neck, for every limb of it ransoms a limb of him from the Fire."""
"19715","223 - al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Murs al narrated to us, saying: Rudayh ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Gharif ibn al-Daylami, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: A group of Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we capture captives and we practise withdrawal from them. He said: ""And do you indeed do that?"" They said: Yes. He said: ""There is no soul that Allah intends to bring forth from the loins of a man but it will come forth, whether he wishes or refuses; so it is no harm upon you not to do so."""
"19716","Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Himsi from Wathilah. 224 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: My uncle Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Himsi, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Among the gravest fabrications is that one claims (descent) to other than one's father, or lies concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or lies concerning one's eyes."""
"19717","Isa ibn Sinan Abu Sinan from Wathilah. 225 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad Isa ibn Sinan, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no man who comes to a soothsayer and asks him but repentance is veiled from him for forty nights; if he believes in what he says, he has disbelieved in Allah."""
"19718","Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari from Wathilah. 226 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Malik al-Fazari narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari narrated to me, saying: I met Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and said: You pledged allegiance with this hand of yours to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: ""Yes."" I said: Give me your hand that I may kiss it. So he gave it to me and I kissed it."
"19719","al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Wathilah. 227 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa, from al-Qasim, from Wathilah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is granted three children and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant (has shown ingratitude for the blessing)."""
"19720","Abu al-Aswad from Wathilah. 228 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us, saying: al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Wathilah, he said: A man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in it alone, and he (the Prophet) moved aside for him. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, the place is spacious. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Muslim has a right."""
"19721","Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn 'Ata' ibn Sulayk narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Wathila, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elderly.'"
"19722","Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawba al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Yazid ibn Rabi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Malik, from Abu al-Azhar, from Wathila ibn al-Asqa', who said: I went out intending to visit 'Ali, and it was said to me: He is with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I headed toward him and found them in an enclosure of reeds, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and 'Ali and Fatima and Hasan and Husayn gathered under a garment, and he said: 'O Allah, You have bestowed Your blessings, mercy, forgiveness, and pleasure upon me and upon them.'"
"19723","'Ubayd al-'Ijl said: Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd ibn Abi Karima al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, who said: Abu al-Fadl narrated to me, from Sinan, the freedman of Wathila, who said: A son of al-Rayyan died, and Wathila attended him. When they returned from the graveyard, Wathila sat at the gate of Damascus, and al-Rayyan passed by him, so Wathila said to him: O Abu Sa'id, may Allah console you in your calamity and forgive your deceased. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Whoever buries three children, Allah forbids the Fire for him.'"
"19724","Isma'il ibn Qirrat al-Dimashqi said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Maqdisi narrated to us, he said: Asma' bint Wathila ibn al-Asqa' narrated to me, she said: My father, when he prayed the dawn prayer, would sit facing the qibla and not speak until the sun rose. Sometimes I would speak to him about some need and he would not speak to me, so I said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Whoever prays the dawn prayer, then recites Say: He is Allah, the One one hundred times before speaking — each time he recites Say: He is Allah, the One, a year of his sins is forgiven.'"
"19725","Isma'il ibn Qirrat narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Asma' bint Wathila narrated to us, from her father, that he used to fast Mondays and Thursdays, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast them, saying: 'Deeds are presented to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, on them.'"
"19726","Isma'il ibn Qirrat narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Asma' bint Wathila narrated to me, from her father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my umma and forbidden for its males.'"
"19727","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki said: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn Yazid, who said: The daughter of Wathila ibn al-Asqa' narrated to me, from her father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves his people — is that tribalism? He said: 'No.' I said: Who is the tribalist? He said: 'The one who aids his people in wrongdoing.'"
"19728","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Khusayla bint Wathila ibn al-Asqa' narrated to us that she heard her father say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is tribalism? He said: 'That you aid your people in wrongdoing.'"
"19729","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi said: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Sadafi narrated to us in the year two hundred and thirty-three, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Ashqar al-Lakhmi narrated to me, he said: Khusayla bint Wathila ibn al-Asqa' narrated to me, she said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Among the gravest of major sins is for a man to attribute to me what I did not say.'"
"19730","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Sadafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Ashqar al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: Khusayla bint Wathila narrated to me, she said: I heard my father say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Among the gravest of major sins is for a man to disown his child.'"
"19731","Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Khusayla bint Wathila narrated to me, she said: I heard my father say: He has succeeded who purifies himself, and remembers the name of his Lord and prays — the giving of wheat on the day of Fitr before the prayer at the prayer ground."
"19732","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Za'ida, (h) and 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: Za'ida narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer in Mecca as two rak'as, the traveler's prayer."
"19733","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara' narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the afternoon prayer at al-Abtah as two rak'as."
"19734","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at al-Abtah with an 'anaza in front of him, or something like an 'anaza, with the road behind it and passersby."
"19735","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward the 'anaza with the road behind it."
"19736","Abu 'Aqil Anas ibn Salim al-Khawlani and Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Musarrih said: al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: When Ja'far came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the land of Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed him between his eyes, then said: 'I do not know whether I am happier at the arrival of Ja'far or at the conquest of Khaybar.'"
"19737","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, that Bilal used to call the adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with each phrase twice, two by two."
"19738","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: Bilal called the adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina in pairs, and the iqama in pairs."
"19739","al-Husayn ibn al-'Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Razi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayer time came. Bilal stood and called the adhan, placing his fingers in his ears and turning around. Water for ablution was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he and his Companions performed ablution; some water remained, and we vied for its remainder. Then an 'anaza was brought out and fixed in the ground, the prayer was announced, and he prayed noon as two rak'as and afternoon as two rak'as toward it. Then he said: 'When I arrive in Medina, come to me.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had assigned us something to give us, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered it to us."
"19740","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw Bilal call the adhan, turning, and I followed his mouth here and there, with his fingers in his ears. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a red tent of his. He said: Bilal came out with the 'anaza in front of him and fixed it at al-Abtah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed noon and afternoon toward it, while dogs, donkeys, and women passed in front of him, wearing a red hulla, as if I am looking at the gleam of his shins."
"19741","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah. Bilal came out and called the adhan, and I watched him, following his mouth here and there — meaning right and left — and he brought out the remainder of his ablution water; people took it, between one who obtained and one who was sprinkled. He fixed an 'anaza, and he came out wearing a red hulla, as if I am looking at the gleam of his shins, and prayed noon and afternoon as two rak'as until he returned."
"19742","Ishaq ibn Jamil narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, that Bilal brought out the remainder of the ablution water of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and people took, between one who obtained and one who was sprinkled, until a boy would slip his hand under people's armpits, dripping."
"19743","Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan al-Kufi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan and Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rak'as, and he kept praying two rak'as until he returned to Medina."
"19744","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed noon at al-Batha' as two rak'as, then traveled and prayed afternoon as two rak'as until he reached Medina, where he prayed in full."
"19745","al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, Abu Humma Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Qurra narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj mentioned, from Abu Khalid, he informed him, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father Abu Juhayfa, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a tent of leather and performed ablution from a stone basin. Bilal came out with the remainder and prayed noon and afternoon; men, women, and donkeys passed in front of him from behind the spear."
"19746","Talib ibn Qurra al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'I do not eat reclining.'"
"19747","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (h) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us — both said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: Bilal came out and fixed an 'anaza, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward it, with donkeys and dogs passing in front of him; and he brought out the remainder of the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And al-Humaydi added in his hadith: and women."
"19748","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah in a tent. Bilal came out and announced the prayer, then Bilal entered and brought out the 'anaza. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, fixed the 'anaza, and the prayer was announced, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for us, with donkeys and women passing in front of him."
"19749","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami and 'Ali ibn al-'Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Akfani narrated to us, Khunays ibn Bakr narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the elderly people of Paradise among the first and the last, apart from the prophets and messengers.'"
"19750","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (h) and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us — both said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj and 'Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at al-Batha' with an 'anaza in front of him, with dogs, donkeys, and women passing beyond it."
"19751","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that Bilal called the adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Batha', placing his fingers in his ears and turning around."
"19752","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: When Bilal called the adhan, he would place his fingers in his ears and turn around during his adhan."
"19753","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw Bilal call the adhan, and I followed his mouth here and there, while Sufyan turned right and left. Yahya said: Sufyan said: Hajjaj used to mention it from 'Awn, that he said: 'And he turned around during his adhan' — but when we met 'Awn, he did not mention 'turned around' in it."
"19754","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) firmly placing his nose on the ground just as he firmly placed his forehead."
"19755","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Nafi' al-Sawariqi narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artat, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warded off the hadd punishment from a woman who was coerced."
"19756","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah in a red tent of his, and he said: 'Who are you?' We said: Banu 'Amir. He said: 'Welcome, you are of me.'"
"19757","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna said: Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and a man of Banu 'Amir, and he said: 'Who are you?' We said: Of Banu 'Amir. He said: 'Welcome to you; you are of me.'"
"19758","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Abtah in a red tent, among a group of Banu 'Amir, and he said to us: 'Of whom are you?' We said: Of Banu 'Amir. He said: 'Then I am of you.' Then Bilal came out and prepared purification water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he called the adhan, placed his fingers in his ears, and turned around during his adhan; and he fixed an 'anaza for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed toward it — noon as two rak'as and afternoon as two rak'as. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: 'Come to me in Medina,' and he promised us salt. We came to Medina and found that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had died, so we went to Abu Bakr, and he fulfilled what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had promised us."
"19759","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa narrated to us, from his father, who said: On the day of departure from Mina we camped at al-Abtah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who announced the prayer. Then the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought out, and the people rushed to it — some obtaining, some being sprinkled. Then he brought out an 'anaza and fixed it between himself and the road."
"19760","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his journey in which they slept through until the sun rose, and he said: 'You were dead, and Allah returned your souls to you. So whoever sleeps through a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes, and whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it.'"
"19761","'Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu 'Ubayda al-'Askari narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mushir narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas al-Hamadani narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When one of you rises from his sleep, let him say: Praise be to Allah who restored our souls to us after we were dead.'"
"19762","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (h) and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I read to Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari — both said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, as far as we know, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The world will be opened to you until you adorn your houses as the Ka'ba is adorned.' We said: While remaining upon our religion? He said: 'Yes; and today you are better than that day.' We said: That day? He said: 'Rather, today you are better.'"
"19763","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us — both said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that a man slaughtered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the Day of Sacrifice, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'It does not suffice for anyone.' He said: I have a jadha'a with me. He said: 'It suffices for you, but it will not suffice anyone after you.'"
"19764","Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, (h) and Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog."
"19765","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the dowry of the prostitute, and the earnings of the cupper."
"19766","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hibban informed us, Salim ibn Qutayba narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and heard someone saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The true call.' Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The word of sincerity.' Then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Its speaker has come out of the Fire.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'You will find him to be a goat-herder or a keeper of dogs, out hunting.'"
"19767","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya, and Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a collector of charity who would take from the rich and give to the poor. Ibn Abi Za'ida said in his hadith: 'And I was an orphan boy, so he gave me a young she-camel from it.'"
"19768","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent among us a collector, who took charity from our rich and gave it to our poor. I was an orphan boy with no wealth, so he gave me a young she-camel from it."
"19769","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, 'Umar ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent — and he mentioned the like."
"19770","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Nafi' narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a boy. While we were camped at Mina, someone said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has departed.' So I stood upon my mount and tightened its saddle, and rode toward him until we reached al-Batha'. There was a small group of people and a pitched tent. Bilal came out to us with ablution water and an 'anaza, then called the adhan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, performed ablution, and left a remainder; people took from it, wiping their faces and heads. I turned and did as they did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the 'anaza in front of him, while people came and went."
"19771","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Abi 'Imran narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as though he saw me awake, for Satan cannot take my likeness.'"
"19772","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Samarqandi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Kufi narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn Abi 'Imran, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever sees me has truly seen me, for Satan cannot resemble me.'"
"19773","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn Abi 'Imran, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like."
"19774","Muhammad ibn Raja' al-Saqati narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Sadir al-Madini narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir ibn Qarawanda narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa narrated to us, from his father, who said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Hajj, and we kept praying two rak'as until we returned."
"19775","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Habib, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man praying with his garment hanging loose, and cut it off for him."
"19776","Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-'Attar narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-'Ala' narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood."
"19777","'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba and al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari narrated to us — they said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Abu al-'Umays narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda'. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda' and found Umm al-Darda' dressed shabbily. He said: What is the matter with you, O Umm al-Darda'? She said: Your brother Abu al-Darda' stands the night in prayer and fasts the day, and has no need of anything of this world. Abu al-Darda' came and welcomed Salman and brought him food. Salman said to him: Eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: I swear to you, you shall break your fast. He refused to eat until he ate with him, so he ate with him. Then he stayed the night with him. During the night Abu al-Darda' wanted to rise, but Salman held him back. Then he said: O Abu al-Darda', your body has a right over you, your Lord has a right, and your family has a right. Give everyone who has a right his right. When it was near dawn, he said: Rise now if you wish. They rose, performed ablution, prayed, then went out to the prayer. Abu al-Darda' approached to inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Your body has a right' — like what Salman had said."
"19778","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Abu al-'Umays, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Abtah; Bilal came and informed him of the prayer — and he mentioned the hadith."
"19779","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, (h) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha' 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — both said: Waki' narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the earnings of the cupper and the dowry of the prostitute."
"19780","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Burda, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Batha'. Bilal had called the adhan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of a tent of his made of leather and sat at its courtyard. Then purification water was brought, and he performed ablution; people hastened to the remainder of his ablution — some drinking, some performing ablution. Then an 'anaza was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and fixed in front of him, and he prayed with the people, while boys, women, sheep, and camels passed in front of him."
"19781","'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us — both said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I saw Bilal come out at midday with an 'anaza and fix it, then stand and call the adhan, placing his fingers in his ears and moving his head like this and like this, right and left, until he finished his adhan. Then he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and brought out a remainder of water; people took, between one who took and one who was sprinkled. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out wearing a red hulla, as if I am looking at the whiteness of his shins beneath it, and prayed toward the 'anaza while travelers passed in front of him. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Bilal."
"19782","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami said: Jubara ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its payer."
"19783","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and two men of Banu 'Amir, and he said: 'Of whom are you?' We said: Of Banu 'Amir. He said: 'You two are of me.'"
"19784","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yunus al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Ja'far al-Farra', from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: An 'anaza used to be fixed for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in open ground, and he would pray toward it."
"19785","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Abu Khalifa said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (h) and Abu Khalifa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us — both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Batha' — an 'anaza was fixed in front of him, and he prayed toward it noon as two rak'as and afternoon as two rak'as, while donkeys and women passed beyond the 'anaza. The wording is that of the hadith of Sulayman ibn Harb."
"19786","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Juhayfa narrating, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at midday to al-Batha', performed ablution, and prayed noon as two rak'as and afternoon as two rak'as, with an 'anaza in front of him. Shu'ba said: 'Awn added, from Abu Juhayfa, he said: Donkeys and women would pass beyond it. Then the people stood and took his hand, wiping their faces with it. I took his hand and placed it on my face, and it was cooler than snow and sweeter in scent than musk."
"19787","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Abu Khalifa said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, who said: I saw my father buy a cupper slave and break his cupping instruments. I asked him about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the price of the dog, and the dowry of the prostitute; and he cursed the tattooer and the one tattooed, and the eater of riba and its payer."
"19788","Abu Khalifa narrated to us, Abu al-Walid and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like — Ibn Kathir added: 'And he cursed the image-maker.'"
"19789","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-Jazari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Anbasa al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu Ma'dan narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa narrating from his father, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a black slave girl, and the woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave to free — does this one suffice for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: 'Where is Allah?' She said: In the heaven. He said: 'Then who am I?' She said: You are His Messenger. He said: 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?' She said: Yes. He said: 'Do you believe in what came from Allah?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Free her, for she is a believer.'"
"19790","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi said: Musaddad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cursed the eater of riba, the tattooer, and the image-maker."
"19791","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: We had a cupper slave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from eating anything of his earnings."
"19792","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karima al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: We camped with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah, and Bilal announced the noon prayer. He came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entered upon him in a house, and brought in with him a basin of water made of leather. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, and some remained in it. Then he came out, and we vied for it. Then Bilal took an 'anaza and fixed it. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed with us two rak'as; I saw women and dogs passing before us while we prayed."
"19793","Abu 'Aruba al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karima narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as though he saw me awake, for Satan cannot take my likeness.'"
"19794","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: Bilal came out at midday and called the adhan, then entered, then came out with a basin containing the remainder of the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), held in his hand — had he placed it on the ground, the people would have broken over it. They took from it — some obtaining, some being sprinkled with the water — and he mentioned the hadith."
"19795","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn 'Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, (h) and 'Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, (h) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah, and I said: I shall observe how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays today. Bilal came out, then entered, then came out with the remainder of the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the people vied for it — some taking, some being sprinkled. Then he entered and brought out an 'anaza and fixed it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out wearing a red hulla, as if I am looking at the whiteness of his shins through it. Bilal announced the prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward, we lined up behind him, and he prayed with us, with donkeys, women, and dogs before him."
"19796","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and al-Hadrami said: Muhammad ibn 'Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out traveling and kept praying two rak'as until he returned."
"19797","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, in the Musnad of Abu Juhayfa, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I prayed noon with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina as two rak'as. al-Hadrami said: This is an error; it is rather Waki', from Sufyan and Ibn Abi Layla."
"19798","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I drew near to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Abtah when the sun had passed its zenith, and Bilal came out and called the adhan for the prayer."
"19799","'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, they said: 'Umar ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa informed us, from his father: that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a red tent of leather. He said: I saw Bilal bring out his ablution water, and I saw the people vie for that ablution water — whoever got some of it wiped himself with it, and whoever got none of it took from the wetness of his companion's hand. Then I saw Bilal bring out an 'anaza and fix it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in a red hulla, his sleeves rolled up, and prayed with the people toward the 'anaza two rak'as; I saw people and animals passing before the 'anaza."
"19800","Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ya'fur narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: I was with my uncle at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and he said: 'The affair of my umma will remain righteous until twelve caliphs have passed' — and he lowered his voice with it. I said to my uncle, who was in front of me: What did he say, uncle? He said: O my son, all of them are of Quraysh."
